/* Generated by tools/build-cert-data.js from tools/cert-source/*.txt. Original ForceNotes practice questions. */
window.FN_CERTS = {"admin":{"id":"admin","short":"Administrator","name":"Salesforce Certified Platform Administrator","blurb":"Configuration, objects, sales and service apps, data and analytics, automation and Agentforce.","exam":{"questions":60,"unscored":"up to 5 unscored","minutes":105,"passing":68,"fee":"US$200 (retake US$100)","release":"Summer '25","guide":"https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=005298966&language=en_US&type=1","trailhead":"https://trailhead.salesforce.com/credentials/administrator"},"domains":[{"n":12,"id":"config","name":"Configuration and Setup","pct":15},{"n":10,"id":"objects","name":"Object Manager and Lightning App Builder","pct":15},{"n":6,"id":"sales","name":"Sales and Marketing Applications","pct":10},{"n":6,"id":"service","name":"Service and Support Applications","pct":10},{"n":6,"id":"productivity","name":"Productivity and Collaboration","pct":10},{"n":13,"id":"data","name":"Data and Analytics Management","pct":17},{"n":10,"id":"automation","name":"Automation","pct":15},{"n":5,"id":"agentforce","name":"Agentforce","pct":8}],"questions":[{"id":"adm-192nd34","d":"config","m":false,"q":"A sales rep has left the company. A new admin wants to remove the rep's user record from the org so it no longer appears anywhere. What should the admin do?","o":["Delete the user record from Setup.","Deactivate the user and reassign the rep's records and automation to other users.","Change the user's username so nobody can log in with it.","Freeze the user, which removes the user from the org and frees the licence."],"a":[1],"e":"Users can never be deleted in Salesforce. They own records and appear in history and audit data, so the correct action is to deactivate them, which also frees the licence, after reassigning their records, approvals and scheduled work. Freezing only blocks login and keeps the licence in use."},{"id":"adm-1jx8e7d","d":"config","m":false,"q":"A company's financial year starts on 1 April. Which Setup setting should the admin review so that forecasts, reports and quota periods follow it?","o":["Business Hours","Default Locale","Fiscal Year","Company Information time zone"],"a":[2],"e":"Fiscal Year settings define when the year starts and how periods are divided, and reports and forecasts use them. Business hours and locale do not affect period boundaries."},{"id":"adm-14w8fnb","d":"config","m":false,"q":"The finance team uses a 4-4-5 week calendar for reporting. What does the admin need to configure?","o":["A custom report type with a bucket field.","A custom fiscal year, instead of a standard fiscal year.","A formula field on every opportunity.","Multiple currencies with dated exchange rates."],"a":[1],"e":"Standard fiscal years follow the Gregorian calendar with a chosen start month. A custom fiscal year lets you define periods such as 4-4-5 weeks."},{"id":"adm-139tooa","d":"config","m":false,"q":"Support cases must be escalated when they have been open for more than 4 hours during the team's working time only, not at night or on weekends. Which setting is used to measure that time?","o":["Fiscal Year","Login Hours","Business Hours (with holidays)","Org-Wide Defaults"],"a":[2],"e":"Business hours (and holidays) define working time. Escalation rules and entitlement milestones use them to decide when time is counting. Login hours only restrict when users can sign in."},{"id":"adm-obxmik","d":"config","m":false,"q":"An admin wants to turn on multiple currencies in production to test it, planning to switch it off again if it does not work out. What should the admin know?","o":["Multiple currencies can be switched off at any time from Company Information.","Multiple currencies can be switched off, but only by Salesforce Support.","Once multiple currencies is enabled it cannot be turned off, so it should be tested in a sandbox first.","Multiple currencies can only be enabled in a sandbox."],"a":[2],"e":"Enabling multiple currencies is permanent. Test it in a sandbox first and plan the corporate currency and exchange rates before enabling it in production."},{"id":"adm-1it2a73","d":"config","m":false,"q":"A new hire in the call centre needs access to custom objects, Accounts, Contacts, reports and dashboards, but will never use Leads, Opportunities or Cases. Which licence type is the best fit?","o":["Salesforce","Salesforce Platform","Identity","Chatter Free"],"a":[1],"e":"The Salesforce Platform user licence is designed for users who work with custom apps and a limited set of standard objects such as Accounts and Contacts, at a lower cost than the full Salesforce licence. A full Salesforce licence gives access to all standard CRM objects."},{"id":"adm-1l5i7lj","d":"config","m":false,"q":"The sales team may only log in from the office network. Which setting enforces this for everyone with the Sales profile?","o":["Trusted IP ranges in Network Access","Login IP ranges on the Sales profile","Session timeout settings","A validation rule on the User object"],"a":[1],"e":"Login IP ranges on a profile block logins from outside those ranges for users with that profile. Org-level trusted IP ranges only let users skip identity verification, they do not block anyone."},{"id":"adm-1rtn4gv","d":"config","m":false,"q":"An admin needs to find out who changed a validation rule last week and when. Where should the admin look?","o":["Field History Tracking","Login History","Setup Audit Trail","Debug Logs"],"a":[2],"e":"The Setup Audit Trail records configuration changes made by admins (who, what and when) and keeps up to 180 days of history. Field History Tracking records data changes on records, not setup changes."},{"id":"adm-tzb9lq","d":"config","m":false,"q":"Opportunities have an organisation-wide default of Private. Sales managers must see their reps' opportunities. What is the simplest solution?","o":["Create a sharing rule for each manager.","Make sure Grant Access Using Hierarchies is selected and place managers above their reps in the role hierarchy.","Change the org-wide default to Public Read Only.","Give managers the View All Data permission."],"a":[1],"e":"With Grant Access Using Hierarchies enabled, users higher in the role hierarchy inherit access to records owned by users below them. It is the least-privilege answer, since changing the default or granting View All Data opens up far more access than needed."},{"id":"adm-1hgfa44","d":"config","m":false,"q":"Support agents have no access to opportunities. A small group of them must be able to view opportunities for healthcare accounts only. The sales model is otherwise Private. Which solution fits?","o":["Move the agents up the role hierarchy.","Give the agents the Modify All permission on Opportunity.","Create a criteria-based sharing rule that shares healthcare opportunities with a public group containing those agents.","Change the opportunity owner to each agent."],"a":[2],"e":"Criteria-based sharing rules open up access to records that match a condition to specific groups, roles or territories. They only extend access, they do not restrict it."},{"id":"adm-1ph48b3","d":"config","m":true,"q":"Which TWO statements about profiles and permission sets are true? (Choose 2)","o":["A user can be assigned many permission sets.","A user can have several profiles.","Every user must have exactly one profile.","Permission sets can remove permissions granted by a profile."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Each user has exactly one profile and any number of permission sets. Permission sets only add access, they cannot take away what the profile already gives. Permissions can be removed only by muting inside a permission set group."},{"id":"adm-ychcj","d":"config","m":false,"q":"A permission set group bundles access for the Service Manager role, but one of the included permission sets grants the Delete permission on Cases, which managers must not have. What is the best way to handle this?","o":["Delete the permission set from the org.","Add a muting permission set to the group that turns off the Delete permission on Cases.","Remove the Delete permission on Cases from the user's profile.","Create a validation rule that blocks case deletion."],"a":[1],"e":"A muting permission set inside a permission set group removes selected permissions for that group only, without changing the other permission sets, so they can still be reused elsewhere."},{"id":"adm-9xahi6","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"A custom object called Course must have many Students, and each Student must be able to attend many Courses. Which design does this?","o":["A lookup from Student to Course.","A master-detail from Course to Student.","A junction object with two master-detail relationships, to Course and to Student.","A hierarchical relationship on Student."],"a":[2],"e":"A many-to-many relationship is modelled with a junction object that has two master-detail relationships, one to each parent."},{"id":"adm-1q9kbsb","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"A custom object has a master-detail relationship to Account. The account is deleted. What happens to the detail records?","o":["They are kept and the Account field is cleared.","They are kept and reassigned to the record owner.","They are deleted along with the account.","Salesforce blocks the delete."],"a":[2],"e":"In a master-detail relationship deleting the master record cascade-deletes its detail records. In a lookup relationship, the child records are kept."},{"id":"adm-1hjuikh","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"A manager asks the admin to delete a custom field used in a validation rule, a formula field and a report. What will happen when the admin tries to delete it?","o":["Salesforce will not allow it until the field is removed from the validation rule and the formula field it is referenced in.","The field is deleted and the validation rule is deactivated automatically.","The field is deleted and formulas that use it return blank.","The field is deleted immediately and cannot be restored."],"a":[0],"e":"Fields referenced by formulas, validation rules, roll-up summaries and similar components must have those references removed first. Deleted fields stay in the recycle area for 15 days and can be restored, unless they are hard-deleted."},{"id":"adm-1ulmu2h","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"An admin tries to convert an existing lookup field on a custom object to a master-detail relationship, but Salesforce shows an error. What is the most likely cause?","o":["The parent object is a custom object.","Some existing child records have an empty value in the lookup field.","The child object has more than one page layout.","The lookup field is marked as searchable."],"a":[1],"e":"A lookup can be converted to master-detail only if every existing record already has a value in the field, because a detail record must always have a parent. The admin should populate the blanks first and then convert it."},{"id":"adm-xdexqz","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"A company wants to show different picklist values and page layouts for its Hardware and Software opportunities, and use a different sales process for each. What should the admin use?","o":["Two page layouts with a dependent picklist.","Record types with separate sales processes and page layouts.","Two profiles with different permission sets.","Two custom objects."],"a":[1],"e":"Record types let one object offer different business processes (such as sales processes), picklist values and page layouts to different users. Page layouts alone only change fields and sections shown."},{"id":"adm-10s3xde","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"A user opens a Lightning record page for Account, but the admin wants a tab to appear only when the account's Type is Customer. Which feature allows this without code?","o":["Profile-level tab settings.","Component visibility filters in Lightning App Builder.","A validation rule.","A custom report type."],"a":[1],"e":"In Lightning App Builder you can set visibility rules on components and tabs, using record fields, user permissions or device, so they appear only when conditions are met."},{"id":"adm-wjkonx","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"An admin wants a visual way to see and create objects and relationships. Which tool should the admin use?","o":["Workbench","Data Loader","Schema Builder","Report Builder"],"a":[2],"e":"Schema Builder is a drag-and-drop tool in Setup that shows objects and their relationships and lets you create custom objects, fields and relationships."},{"id":"adm-c1pojz","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"The admin adds a new field but the users still cannot see it on the Contact page. The field-level security is set correctly. What is the most likely cause?","o":["The field is a lookup.","The field has not been added to the page layout or Lightning record page that the users see.","The users need a new licence.","The field must first be indexed."],"a":[1],"e":"Field-level security controls whether users can access the field, but they still only see it when it is placed on the page layout (or a Dynamic Forms page) they are assigned."},{"id":"adm-w058d7","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"A picklist field for Country must control the values available in a second picklist, State. What feature should the admin use?","o":["A global value set.","A formula field.","A dependent picklist (field dependency).","A record type."],"a":[2],"e":"Dependent picklists use a controlling field to filter which values appear in the dependent field."},{"id":"adm-1xt1mks","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"A quick action should let users create a Case from an Account record with some fields pre-populated. What should the admin configure?","o":["An object-specific quick action on Account that creates a Case, with predefined field values.","A global quick action only.","A custom button that opens a URL.","A validation rule."],"a":[0],"e":"Object-specific quick actions can create related records with fields prepopulated. Global actions can create records but are not tied to a parent record in the same way."},{"id":"adm-198n7bo","d":"sales","m":false,"q":"A sales director wants reps to see the stages of the sales process at the top of each opportunity, with key fields and guidance for each stage. What should the admin set up?","o":["A dashboard component.","A validation rule for each stage.","Path for Opportunities.","An approval process."],"a":[2],"e":"Path shows the stages of a process across the top of a record and can show key fields and guidance for each stage."},{"id":"adm-tiza68","d":"sales","m":false,"q":"A rep converts a qualified lead. Which records can Salesforce create or match as part of the conversion?","o":["A case and a contract","A campaign and a quote","An account and a contact, and optionally an opportunity","An opportunity only"],"a":[2],"e":"Lead conversion creates (or matches) an account and a contact, and the rep can also choose to create an opportunity. Lead field mapping decides how lead data copies into the new records."},{"id":"adm-dadjd8","d":"sales","m":false,"q":"Leads from the website should be distributed to a regional team automatically based on the lead's country. What should the admin use?","o":["A queue with an approval process.","Lead assignment rules.","A sharing rule.","A dynamic dashboard."],"a":[1],"e":"Lead assignment rules assign leads to users or queues based on criteria such as country. Only one assignment rule can be active at a time."},{"id":"adm-zc1xr0","d":"sales","m":false,"q":"A marketing manager wants to track which contacts and leads responded to an email campaign. What should be used?","o":["A report type.","A custom object.","Campaign members.","A lead queue."],"a":[2],"e":"Campaign members are the leads and contacts connected to a campaign, with a status that shows whether they responded."},{"id":"adm-1nlbb40","d":"sales","m":false,"q":"Sales leadership wants predicted revenue by rep, rolled up through the management hierarchy, based on opportunity stage and amount. Which feature supports this?","o":["Dashboards with a running user.","Collaborative Forecasts.","Territory-based sharing rules.","Lead scoring."],"a":[1],"e":"Forecasts roll up opportunity data by user and forecast category through the role hierarchy (or territory hierarchy), giving managers a view of expected revenue."},{"id":"adm-rrnter","d":"sales","m":false,"q":"Two sales regions need separate account access that does not follow the role hierarchy, such as accounts assigned by industry and geography. Which feature should the admin consider?","o":["Public groups","Opportunity teams","Enterprise Territory Management.","Record types"],"a":[2],"e":"Territory management lets you organise accounts by criteria like geography and industry in a hierarchy of territories, independently of the role hierarchy, and assign users to them."},{"id":"adm-a26lhu","d":"service","m":false,"q":"A support team shares one pool of unassigned cases, and any agent should be able to pick up a case from it. Which feature supports this?","o":["A public group.","A role hierarchy.","A queue.","A permission set."],"a":[2],"e":"Queues hold records until a member takes ownership, and cases can be routed to a queue through assignment rules."},{"id":"adm-1kou2zj","d":"service","m":false,"q":"Support wants every customer who emails a question to receive an immediate acknowledgement that includes the case number. What should the admin use?","o":["An escalation rule.","A validation rule.","A case auto-response rule.","A support process."],"a":[2],"e":"Auto-response rules send email responses to people who submit cases from sources like Web-to-Case or Email-to-Case, using a template that can include merge fields such as the case number."},{"id":"adm-zf7jhc","d":"service","m":false,"q":"Cases unresolved after 8 business hours must be reassigned to a senior queue and the manager notified. Which feature does this?","o":["Case assignment rules.","Case escalation rules.","Case auto-response rules.","Public groups."],"a":[1],"e":"Escalation rules reassign and notify when cases have not been resolved within the time defined, using business hours if configured."},{"id":"adm-nulnx9","d":"service","m":false,"q":"Different case statuses must be available to technical support and billing support. What should the admin configure?","o":["Support processes with record types.","Two page layouts on the Case object.","A dependent picklist.","A queue per status."],"a":[0],"e":"A support process defines the case Status values available, and it is assigned through a record type, so each team sees only the statuses that apply to them."},{"id":"adm-11pn04d","d":"service","m":false,"q":"Customers email support@company.com and a case should be created for each email automatically. Which feature should be set up?","o":["Web-to-Case.","Email-to-Case.","Auto-response rules.","A flow that polls a mailbox."],"a":[1],"e":"Email-to-Case turns inbound emails into cases and attaches the email to the case."},{"id":"adm-qm633p","d":"service","m":false,"q":"A support manager wants service agents to see suggested answers from a knowledge base while working on cases. What do the agents need?","o":["A Chatter group.","Salesforce Knowledge articles and the Knowledge component on the case page.","A dashboard.","A custom report type."],"a":[1],"e":"Salesforce Knowledge stores articles that agents search or that are suggested on the case page through the Knowledge component."},{"id":"adm-1ecfclc","d":"productivity","m":false,"q":"What is the difference between a task and an event in Salesforce?","o":["Tasks have a start and end time, and events do not.","An event is scheduled for a specific date and time on a calendar, while a task is a to-do item with a due date.","Tasks can only be related to leads.","Events cannot be related to accounts."],"a":[1],"e":"Events appear on the calendar with a start and end time (meetings, calls booked in advance). Tasks are to-dos with a due date and status that are not time-boxed."},{"id":"adm-16ganwm","d":"productivity","m":false,"q":"A department wants a Chatter group where only approved members can read the posts and files. Other employees may see that the group exists. Which group type is right?","o":["Public","Private","Broadcast-only, with all users as members","A public group from Setup"],"a":[1],"e":"In a private Chatter group only members can see the posts and files, while non-members can see only the group's name and description. In a public Chatter group any internal user can see and join. A \"public group\" in Setup is a different feature used for sharing."},{"id":"adm-33f14c","d":"productivity","m":false,"q":"An admin wants users in the Salesforce mobile app to see only the five most important tabs. What should the admin edit?","o":["The profile's Tab Settings.","The mobile app navigation menu in Setup.","The home page layout.","The page layout for Account."],"a":[1],"e":"The Salesforce mobile app navigation menu controls the items in the mobile app's navigation, and the admin can set the order and which items appear."},{"id":"adm-qf225i","d":"productivity","m":true,"q":"What is the difference between a managed package and an unmanaged package? (Choose 2)","o":["Managed packages can be upgraded by the publisher and the code is hidden from the subscriber.","Unmanaged packages can only be installed by the publisher's own users.","Unmanaged packages are a one-time distribution, and once installed the components can be edited by the subscriber.","Managed packages must be built by the subscriber."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Managed packages are released by publishers (typically ISVs) with upgrade paths and protected code. Unmanaged packages copy components into the subscriber's org as editable, with no upgrade path."},{"id":"adm-19k4gy3","d":"productivity","m":false,"q":"Where would an admin find ready-to-install apps, components and prompts built by Salesforce partners?","o":["Setup Audit Trail","Developer Console","The AppExchange (including AgentExchange for agent assets).","Trailhead"],"a":[2],"e":"The AppExchange is Salesforce's marketplace for partner solutions, and AgentExchange covers agent-related assets such as prompts and actions."},{"id":"adm-k5z8xo","d":"productivity","m":false,"q":"When an admin wants to log in as another user to troubleshoot a problem, what permission setting must usually be in place?","o":["The user must reset their password.","The user must grant login access to the admin, or the org must allow admins to log in as any user.","The admin must clone the user's profile.","The admin must run a debug log."],"a":[1],"e":"Login access settings control whether admins can log in as other users, and users can grant access for a period from their own settings."},{"id":"adm-1twotxt","d":"data","m":false,"q":"An admin needs to load 40,000 new contacts with a few relationship fields. The admin is not comfortable with command-line tools and wants a guided experience. Which tool fits best?","o":["Data Import Wizard.","Workbench with SOQL.","Data Loader with the Bulk API only.","Change sets."],"a":[0],"e":"The Data Import Wizard handles up to 50,000 records at a time for supported objects such as contacts, leads and accounts, with a guided interface. Data Loader suits larger volumes or objects the wizard does not support."},{"id":"adm-maydoh","d":"data","m":false,"q":"An admin must insert, update and delete up to 2 million records and run scheduled loads. Which tool should be used?","o":["Data Import Wizard.","Report Export.","Data Loader.","Quick actions."],"a":[2],"e":"Data Loader is a client application that handles very large volumes (up to millions of records), and it supports insert, update, upsert, delete, hard delete and export, plus command-line scheduling."},{"id":"adm-19uufj0","d":"data","m":true,"q":"Duplicate leads keep being created. The admin wants to warn users when they create a lead that looks like an existing record. What two features work together to do this? (Choose 2)","o":["A matching rule to define which fields indicate a duplicate.","A sharing rule to hide existing leads.","A duplicate rule that decides what happens when a match is found.","A validation rule that checks the lead's email format."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Matching rules decide how to identify duplicates, and duplicate rules decide the action, which can be to alert or to block the save."},{"id":"adm-zisno3","d":"data","m":false,"q":"Users must not be able to save an opportunity with a Close Date in the past. Which feature enforces this without code?","o":["A field-level security setting.","A page layout setting.","A validation rule.","A report filter."],"a":[2],"e":"Validation rules evaluate when a record is saved and block the save with an error message when the formula returns true."},{"id":"adm-1qimc46","d":"data","m":false,"q":"A report has to show accounts with and without opportunities. Which option should the admin choose when creating a custom report type?","o":["Each A record must have at least one B record.","A records may or may not have B records.","Only the primary object.","Joined report."],"a":[1],"e":"Choosing that A records may or may not have B records produces an outer join, so accounts without opportunities still appear in the report."},{"id":"adm-bo9dmj","d":"data","m":false,"q":"Sales reps want to group opportunity amounts into small, medium and large buckets without creating a new field. What should they use?","o":["A formula field.","A bucket field in the report.","A roll-up summary field.","A picklist."],"a":[1],"e":"Bucket fields categorise report values on the fly and exist only inside the report, no field is created."},{"id":"adm-365ajc","d":"data","m":false,"q":"A manager wants to compare two different report blocks side by side, such as opportunities and cases for the same account. Which report format fits?","o":["Tabular","Summary","Matrix","Joined"],"a":[3],"e":"Joined reports let you view different types of information in one report using blocks, each block based on a report type."},{"id":"adm-1y0jw1e","d":"data","m":false,"q":"Each sales rep must see a dashboard showing only their own pipeline, using the same dashboard. What should the admin set?","o":["Dashboard running user as the admin.","A dynamic dashboard, where data is shown according to the access of the viewing user.","A scheduled dashboard refresh.","A matrix report."],"a":[1],"e":"With a dynamic dashboard, the dashboard runs as the viewing user, so each person sees data they have access to."},{"id":"adm-fdqh2s","d":"data","m":false,"q":"A user cannot see a report in a folder where their colleague can. The user has access to the report type and the data. What should the admin check?","o":["Dashboard subscriptions.","Whether the user has access to the report folder, for example as a Viewer.","The user's time zone.","The report's chart type."],"a":[1],"e":"Reports and dashboards are shared through folders. Users need folder access in addition to access to the underlying data and report type."},{"id":"adm-1i0j9rp","d":"data","m":false,"q":"A company wants a recurring backup of its Salesforce data as files it can store elsewhere. Which built-in feature should the admin use?","o":["Data Import Wizard","Change sets","Dashboard subscriptions","Data Export (scheduled export) in Setup"],"a":[3],"e":"Data Export lets admins schedule exports of data (and files) as CSV files on a regular basis, which supports backups. Import tools bring data in, change sets move metadata, and subscriptions only email dashboard snapshots."},{"id":"adm-8cao2n","d":"data","m":false,"q":"An admin deleted 500 accounts by mistake yesterday using a mass delete. How can the admin most easily recover them?","o":["Restore them from a change set.","Restore them from the Recycle Bin.","Re-run Setup Audit Trail.","Ask users to re-enter them."],"a":[1],"e":"Deleted records go to the Recycle Bin for 15 days, where they can be restored, unless they were hard-deleted."},{"id":"adm-9c0th5","d":"data","m":true,"q":"Which TWO features are used to improve data quality when users enter records? (Choose 2)","o":["Validation rules","Dashboards","Duplicate rules","Chatter feeds"],"a":[0,2],"e":"Validation rules and duplicate rules check or alert on data as users save records."},{"id":"adm-13p3xi3","d":"data","m":false,"q":"Users report that a dashboard shows data they should not have access to. The dashboard running user is a system administrator. What is the most likely reason?","o":["The dashboard runs as a fixed user, so everyone sees the data the running user can see.","The dashboard is dynamic.","The report type is standard.","The dashboard has no subscription."],"a":[0],"e":"A dashboard run as a specified user shows all viewers the same data that user can see, regardless of the viewers' own access."},{"id":"adm-veaspm","d":"automation","m":false,"q":"A company wants to automatically update the account's rating when an opportunity is closed won, with no code. Which tool is recommended for this?","o":["Workflow rule","Process Builder","Record-triggered flow","Approval process"],"a":[2],"e":"Flow is Salesforce's automation tool for new work, and Workflow Rules and Process Builder have been retired. A record-triggered flow can update related records when an opportunity changes."},{"id":"adm-1q3ba89","d":"automation","m":false,"q":"A guided process asks a user questions on screen and creates a case based on the answers. Which flow type should be used?","o":["Record-triggered flow","Scheduled-triggered flow","Screen flow","Platform event-triggered flow"],"a":[2],"e":"Screen flows present a user interface with screens and inputs, and they can create or update records based on what the user enters."},{"id":"adm-11lkygg","d":"automation","m":false,"q":"A flow must run every night to close all tasks overdue by more than 30 days. Which flow type fits?","o":["Screen flow","Record-triggered flow","Scheduled-triggered flow","Autolaunched flow called by a button"],"a":[2],"e":"Scheduled-triggered flows run at a set time and frequency against a batch of records that match filters."},{"id":"adm-uwk6nw","d":"automation","m":false,"q":"Which statement about the order of execution when a record is saved is correct?","o":["Custom validation rules run before before-save flows.","After-save flows run before the record is written to the database.","Before-save record-triggered flows run first, then before triggers, then validation rules, and after-save automation runs after the record has been saved (but not yet committed).","Assignment rules run before any triggers or flows."],"a":[2],"e":"The save order is: before-save flows, before triggers, system and custom validation, duplicate rules, the record is saved (not committed), after triggers, assignment and auto-response rules, escalation rules, after-save flows, and finally the commit. Knowing this helps predict why automation behaves as it does."},{"id":"adm-u9myvb","d":"automation","m":false,"q":"Opportunities over $100,000 must be approved by a regional manager, and the record must be locked while waiting. What is the best tool?","o":["A validation rule","An approval process","A scheduled flow","Record types"],"a":[1],"e":"Approval processes route records for approval, can lock the record while pending, and track approvers, approvals and rejections."},{"id":"adm-o0lt0r","d":"automation","m":false,"q":"A new lead should be assigned to the correct sales rep by region. Another admin suggests a flow, but there is already an active lead assignment rule. What is the best advice?","o":["Use the lead assignment rule, since it is designed for this and is simpler to maintain.","Always use a flow, because assignment rules are retired.","Build a validation rule.","Use a workflow rule."],"a":[0],"e":"Choose the simplest declarative tool that does the job. Lead assignment rules are purpose-built for routing leads, so there is no need for a flow unless the logic is too complex for them."},{"id":"adm-1rmzd1c","d":"automation","m":false,"q":"A record-triggered flow updates the account the same record is related to, and then the account update starts another flow that updates the original record. What risk should the admin consider?","o":["Validation rules will be ignored.","A loop of updates that can hit limits or cause errors, so entry conditions and the order of execution must be planned.","Flows cannot update records.","The flows will merge automatically."],"a":[1],"e":"Automation that updates records can trigger other automation. Entry conditions and \"only when a record is updated to meet the condition\" settings help prevent recursion."},{"id":"adm-10cl4ic","d":"automation","m":false,"q":"A flow fails for some users in production, and the admin received an error email. Where can the admin find more detail?","o":["The Setup Audit Trail.","The flow's error email and Paused and Failed Flow Interviews, plus the debug option in Flow Builder.","The Data Import Wizard.","The report type list."],"a":[1],"e":"Flow errors are emailed to the admin, failed and paused interviews can be reviewed in Setup, and Flow Builder's Debug lets you test with specific records and see each element's result."},{"id":"adm-1725ahf","d":"automation","m":false,"q":"A flow must run before a record is saved to set a field value quickly, with no extra database update. Which setting does this?","o":["After-save record-triggered flow.","Before-save (fast field updates) record-triggered flow.","Autolaunched flow.","Scheduled flow."],"a":[1],"e":"Before-save flows update the triggering record's fields without a separate database operation, which makes them faster than after-save flows."},{"id":"adm-17n6322","d":"automation","m":true,"q":"Which TWO factors should an admin consider when choosing between a flow and an approval process? (Choose 2)","o":["Whether the record must be locked and routed through a formal sign-off.","Which tool has a nicer colour scheme.","Whether the logic goes beyond routing for approval, such as creating records on approval.","Whether the user has a mobile phone."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Approval processes are best when you need formal submissions, approvers and record locking, and flows (including flow approval features) handle broader logic."},{"id":"adm-1g3dmyp","d":"agentforce","m":false,"q":"A company wants an AI agent that answers customer questions about orders using the company's data. What is the main building block that defines what an agent can do?","o":["Topics with instructions and actions.","A page layout.","A queue.","A permission set group."],"a":[0],"e":"An Agentforce agent is configured with topics (areas of responsibility), instructions for how to handle them, and actions (flows, Apex, prompt templates) it can run."},{"id":"adm-6065ls","d":"agentforce","m":false,"q":"An admin wants to test how an agent responds to sample questions before releasing it. Where can this be done?","o":["In Agent Builder, using the conversation preview.","In the Data Import Wizard.","In Schema Builder.","In Setup Audit Trail."],"a":[0],"e":"Agent Builder lets you configure the agent and test it in a conversation preview before you activate it."},{"id":"adm-fi0l1f","d":"agentforce","m":false,"q":"An agent cannot update a record when users ask it to. The flow works when run by an admin. What should the admin check first?","o":["The permissions of the agent's running user, such as object and field access.","The browser used by the customer.","The size of the dashboard.","The fiscal year."],"a":[0],"e":"The agent acts under a user context, so missing object, field or flow permissions will stop actions that work for an admin."},{"id":"adm-jwj7fc","d":"agentforce","m":false,"q":"When is an AI agent a good fit compared with a standard flow?","o":["When the steps are fixed and never change.","When requests are expressed in natural language and vary, so the system needs to decide which action to take.","Whenever data needs to be exported.","Only when the org has no automation."],"a":[1],"e":"Fixed, predictable steps are usually best as flows, while agents suit flexible, language-driven requests that need reasoning about which action to run."},{"id":"adm-12v8faf","d":"agentforce","m":false,"q":"What is the purpose of the Einstein Trust Layer for AI features?","o":["It hides records from users.","It adds protections such as masking sensitive data and not retaining customer data, when prompts go to a large language model.","It speeds up reports.","It replaces sharing rules."],"a":[1],"e":"The Einstein Trust Layer sits between Salesforce data and the model provider and applies protections such as data masking, zero data retention and toxicity checks."}]},"appbuilder":{"id":"appbuilder","short":"App Builder","name":"Salesforce Certified Platform App Builder","blurb":"Fundamentals, data modeling, business logic and Flow, user interface and app deployment.","exam":{"questions":60,"unscored":"up to 5 unscored","minutes":105,"passing":73,"fee":"US$200 (retake US$100)","release":"SU '26","guide":"https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=005298964&language=en_US&type=1","trailhead":"https://trailhead.salesforce.com/credentials/platformappbuilder"},"domains":[{"n":13,"id":"fundamentals","name":"Salesforce Fundamentals","pct":18},{"n":13,"id":"data","name":"Data Modeling and Management","pct":20},{"n":19,"id":"logic","name":"Business Logic and Process Automation","pct":32},{"n":11,"id":"ui","name":"User Interface","pct":17},{"n":8,"id":"deploy","name":"App Deployment","pct":13}],"questions":[{"id":"app-48mzr5","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"A company needs to calculate a customer score by running a complex, multi-step algorithm with loops and calls to an external pricing service during a nightly job. Which approach is best?","o":["A formula field","A screen flow with a decision element","Programmatic customisation, such as Apex, because the requirement goes beyond what declarative tools handle well","A validation rule"],"a":[2],"e":"Declarative tools such as formulas, validation rules and flows cover most requirements. Complex logic with heavy iteration and external service calls, especially in bulk, is the kind of requirement where code is a better fit."},{"id":"app-f894il","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"The business wants an e-signature capability for contracts. Building it from scratch would take months. What should the app builder recommend?","o":["Build a custom Lightning web component.","Look for a solution on AppExchange (or AgentExchange) that already provides it.","Create a custom object called Signature.","Use a validation rule that requires a signature field."],"a":[1],"e":"Extending the org with a partner solution is often faster and cheaper than building common capabilities from scratch. Evaluate fit, security, cost and support before installing."},{"id":"app-tn9lqp","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"Employees should be able to see an Employee record but not its Salary field. Which feature enforces this everywhere, including reports and the API?","o":["Removing the field from the page layout","Field-level security on the Salary field","A validation rule","A record type"],"a":[1],"e":"Page layouts only control what is shown on the page. Field-level security restricts access to the field in the UI, reports, list views and the API."},{"id":"app-1s5ddmo","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"A small group of service reps needs the Delete permission on Cases, but their profile does not grant it and other reps with the same profile must not get it. What is the best solution?","o":["Edit the shared profile to add Delete.","Create a permission set with Delete on Cases and assign it to those reps.","Change the organisation-wide default for Cases.","Create a new role above everyone."],"a":[1],"e":"Permission sets extend access for selected users without changing the profile everybody shares."},{"id":"app-8zios9","d":"fundamentals","m":true,"q":"Which TWO features can open up record access beyond the organisation-wide default? (Choose 2)","o":["Sharing rules","Field-level security","Manual sharing","Page layouts"],"a":[0,2],"e":"Organisation-wide defaults set the most restrictive baseline. Sharing rules, manual sharing, the role hierarchy, teams and similar features can only grant more access on top of it."},{"id":"app-13hkm2o","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"Accounts are Private. Reps working on the same large account need temporary access to it, and the account owner decides who. What is the simplest feature?","o":["A criteria-based sharing rule","Account teams (or manual sharing by the owner)","A new profile","Territory hierarchy"],"a":[1],"e":"The record owner can add colleagues to an account team or share the record manually to give access to specific people when needed."},{"id":"app-8ri3z8","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"A report must show Accounts together with their Contacts and the Cases of those Accounts. No standard report type provides all three. What should the app builder create?","o":["A joined report with three blocks.","A custom report type that includes the three related objects.","A new dashboard.","Three tabular reports."],"a":[1],"e":"Custom report types let you define which objects and relationships a report can use. Standard types cover common relationships only."},{"id":"app-nkza81","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"Executives must see a dashboard that includes data from records they cannot open themselves. What dashboard setting allows this?","o":["Dynamic dashboard","A fixed running user who has access to that data","A dashboard subscription","A dashboard filter"],"a":[1],"e":"With a fixed running user, every viewer sees the data that user can access. It is appropriate when viewers should see summarised data they do not have record access to, and the running user should have no more access than needed."},{"id":"app-1o3kxnb","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"Viewers of a sales dashboard want to narrow all components by region without editing the dashboard. What should the app builder add?","o":["A dashboard filter on Region","A bucket field","A joined report","A new report type"],"a":[0],"e":"Dashboard filters let viewers filter all components at once using fields that exist in the underlying reports."},{"id":"app-xrpwj8","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"Users can see a field on the page layout as read-only, but a data integration still updates it. The business wants nobody but admins to edit it through any route. What should be used?","o":["Make it read-only in the page layout","Restrict edit access with field-level security","Hide it with a record type","Add a validation rule on the profile"],"a":[1],"e":"A read-only page layout setting only affects the UI. Field-level security is enforced everywhere, including the API and imports."},{"id":"app-6k5og6","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"An organisation-wide default of Private for Opportunities means which of the following?","o":["Everyone can view but not edit all opportunities.","Users can see only the opportunities they own, plus those shared with them or visible through other sharing features.","Only admins can see opportunities.","Opportunities are hidden from the role hierarchy."],"a":[1],"e":"Private is the most restrictive default. Users get access through ownership, the role hierarchy, sharing rules, teams and manual sharing."},{"id":"app-5x2pwx","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"Which requirement can an app builder meet declaratively without writing any code? (Choose the best answer)","o":["Making a callout to an external system from a database trigger.","Updating a related account whenever an opportunity is closed won.","Running custom Apex batch processing on 10 million records.","Building a custom UI framework with its own routing."],"a":[1],"e":"A record-triggered flow can update related records. Callouts from triggers, large-scale batch processing and custom frameworks are programmatic territory."},{"id":"app-1hyirel","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"A company wants sales reps to see a list of related records on the account page, filtered to open cases only. Which declarative option fits?","o":["A related list component with a filter on the Lightning record page","An Apex controller","A new object","A validation rule"],"a":[0],"e":"In Lightning App Builder, related list components can be configured, including which columns and filters appear, without code."},{"id":"app-qyqiy","d":"data","m":false,"q":"A school needs a student to be enrolled in many courses and each course to have many students, with a grade stored for each enrolment. What data model fits?","o":["A lookup from Student to Course","A junction object (Enrolment) with master-detail relationships to Student and Course, holding the grade","A hierarchical relationship on Student","A text field with the course names"],"a":[1],"e":"Many-to-many relationships use a junction object with two master-detail relationships. The junction record holds data about the pairing, such as the grade."},{"id":"app-1egdku3","d":"data","m":false,"q":"Child records must be able to exist without a parent, and each child needs its own owner. Which relationship type should be used?","o":["Master-detail","Lookup","Hierarchical","External lookup"],"a":[1],"e":"A lookup is a loose relationship: the parent is optional, and the child keeps its own owner and sharing. A master-detail child inherits access from the parent and cannot exist without it."},{"id":"app-pyo95d","d":"data","m":false,"q":"A business needs the total of all child order line amounts shown on the parent Order record. The relationship between them is a lookup. Which is the best declarative solution?","o":["A roll-up summary field","A formula field","A record-triggered flow that recalculates the total","A validation rule"],"a":[2],"e":"Roll-up summary fields are available only on the master side of a master-detail relationship. For a lookup relationship, a flow (or an AppExchange tool) can calculate the total."},{"id":"app-1y3ju92","d":"data","m":false,"q":"What is a consequence of a master-detail relationship between a parent and a child object?","o":["The child record's owner and sharing are controlled by the parent, and deleting the parent deletes the children.","The child can have its own owner and its own sharing rules.","The relationship can be blank on the child.","The parent can be a child of the same object."],"a":[0],"e":"In a master-detail relationship the detail inherits ownership and sharing from the master and is deleted with it, and the master field is required."},{"id":"app-ykeuqn","d":"data","m":false,"q":"Which relationship is available only for the User object and lets you build a management chain?","o":["Many-to-many","Self relationship","Hierarchical relationship","External lookup"],"a":[2],"e":"Hierarchical relationships exist only on the User object. They are a special kind of lookup, for example to model who reports to whom."},{"id":"app-toj319","d":"data","m":false,"q":"A company wants to show accounts in a parent and subsidiary structure. How is this achieved on the Account object?","o":["Use the Parent Account lookup, which is a self-relationship on Account.","Create a junction object between Account and Account.","Use a hierarchical relationship.","Create a roll-up summary field."],"a":[0],"e":"Account has a standard lookup to itself (Parent Account) that builds the account hierarchy."},{"id":"app-1snqepy","d":"data","m":false,"q":"Data about invoices lives in an external billing system. Users want to see invoices on the Account page in real time without importing them. Which feature should be used?","o":["Data Loader scheduled daily","Salesforce Connect with external objects","A custom object with a nightly flow","Data Import Wizard"],"a":[1],"e":"External objects (through Salesforce Connect) show data stored outside Salesforce without copying it, and can be related to Salesforce records with external or indirect lookups."},{"id":"app-12ufa4w","d":"data","m":false,"q":"A text field called Customer Number has some values that contain letters. An admin changes the field type to Number. What is the expected result?","o":["Salesforce keeps all values as they are.","Values that are not numeric are lost, so the admin should export the data first.","The field is converted to a lookup.","Salesforce blocks the change in all cases."],"a":[1],"e":"Changing a field data type can delete or change data that does not fit the new type. Always back up data and review the considerations before changing a type."},{"id":"app-dbck6t","d":"data","m":false,"q":"An external system sends a unique customer ID. The team wants to match records on that ID during imports and avoid creating duplicates. What should the app builder create?","o":["A formula field","A roll-up summary field","A text field marked as External ID (and unique), used with upsert","A global value set"],"a":[2],"e":"An External ID field lets tools such as Data Loader match records on an ID from another system during upsert operations."},{"id":"app-13ltel2","d":"data","m":false,"q":"A Contact lookup on the Case object should show only contacts that belong to the case's account. What feature does this declaratively?","o":["A lookup filter","A validation rule only","A record type","A page layout"],"a":[0],"e":"Lookup filters limit which records can be selected in a lookup field, and can reference fields from the current record, such as the account."},{"id":"app-ztogj3","d":"data","m":false,"q":"A field stores a price with two decimal places and must work with the org's currencies. Which data type should be used?","o":["Number","Text","Currency","Percent"],"a":[2],"e":"Currency fields store monetary values and, with multi-currency enabled, are converted according to the exchange rates."},{"id":"app-sabd7k","d":"data","m":true,"q":"Which TWO statements describe a junction object? (Choose 2)","o":["It has two master-detail relationships.","It always has its own independent owner.","Deleting one of its masters deletes the related junction records.","It cannot have custom fields."],"a":[0,2],"e":"A junction object resolves many-to-many relationships through two master-detail fields. The junction records are removed when either master record is deleted, and they can have their own custom fields."},{"id":"app-prratb","d":"data","m":false,"q":"Data about 300,000 records must be loaded into a new custom object, then the data owner will update the same records weekly with changed values. Which approach is best?","o":["Insert the data again every week.","Load with Data Loader, then use upsert with an External ID for the weekly updates.","Use the Data Import Wizard for both loads.","Create the records manually."],"a":[1],"e":"Upsert uses an External ID to insert new records and update existing ones in a single operation, so weekly updates do not create duplicates. The Import Wizard handles up to 50,000 records at a time."},{"id":"app-z37l2g","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"Which formula correctly returns TRUE when the Opportunity Stage picklist is Closed Won?","o":["StageName = \"Closed Won\"","ISPICKVAL(StageName, \"Closed Won\")","CONTAINS(StageName, \"Closed Won\")","StageName == \"Closed Won\" && TRUE"],"a":[1],"e":"Picklist fields cannot be compared with plain operators in formulas. Use ISPICKVAL() (or wrap the field in TEXT() first)."},{"id":"app-1d9tql2","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"An app builder wants an Opportunity field that shows the Account's Industry. What kind of field should be created?","o":["A roll-up summary field","A cross-object formula field that references Account.Industry","A lookup field","A flow variable"],"a":[1],"e":"A formula field can reference fields on a related parent record through relationship fields, so it always shows the current value."},{"id":"app-13jpwuc","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A formula field must show the number of days between today and the Close Date. Which formula returns that value?","o":["CloseDate - TODAY()","TODAY() + CloseDate","DATEVALUE(CloseDate)","CloseDate + 1"],"a":[0],"e":"Subtracting dates in a formula returns a number of days. The return type of the formula field should be Number."},{"id":"app-1sd0b4i","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A text field must default to a date thirty days from today for new records. What should the app builder use?","o":["A validation rule","A default value formula such as TODAY() + 30","A roll-up summary field","A cross-object formula"],"a":[1],"e":"Default values can be set with a formula that is evaluated when a record is created."},{"id":"app-p8mbye","d":"logic","m":true,"q":"Which statements about roll-up summary fields are true? (Choose 2)","o":["They can calculate COUNT, SUM, MIN and MAX of child records.","They can be created on any lookup relationship.","They can use filter criteria to include only some child records.","They can calculate the average of child values."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Roll-up summary fields work on the master side of master-detail relationships and support COUNT, SUM, MIN and MAX, with optional filters. Averages are not supported."},{"id":"app-ng7n16","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A roll-up summary should add up only those opportunity products that are marked as Active. What should the app builder configure?","o":["A separate report","A filter criteria on the roll-up summary field","A validation rule","A formula on the child object only"],"a":[1],"e":"Roll-up summary fields can include filter criteria so that only matching child records are counted or summed."},{"id":"app-1wex3k9","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A business rule says: when the Stage is Closed Lost, the Loss Reason field must be completed. Which validation rule formula enforces that?","o":["ISPICKVAL(StageName, \"Closed Lost\") && ISBLANK(Loss_Reason__c) == FALSE","AND(ISPICKVAL(StageName, \"Closed Lost\"), ISBLANK(Loss_Reason__c))","OR(ISPICKVAL(StageName, \"Closed Lost\"), ISBLANK(Loss_Reason__c))","NOT(ISPICKVAL(StageName, \"Closed Lost\"))"],"a":[1],"e":"A validation rule blocks the save when its formula returns TRUE. The rule must be true when the stage is Closed Lost AND the loss reason is blank."},{"id":"app-atln01","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"An integration user loads records and must be allowed to save data that breaks a validation rule used by human users. What is the best approach?","o":["Delete the validation rule.","Deactivate the rule during every load.","Add a custom permission check to the rule and assign it to the integration user through a permission set.","Give the integration user the Modify All Data permission."],"a":[2],"e":"A bypass based on a custom permission is auditable and targeted, and it avoids switching rules on and off."},{"id":"app-6wc9ng","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A validation rule on Lead is configured to require a mobile number, but it does not fire when a lead is converted. What should the app builder check?","o":["The Lead setting that requires validation for converted leads","The profile's login hours","The lead assignment rule","The page layout"],"a":[0],"e":"By default validation rules do not run on lead conversion, and the setting to require validation for converted leads must be enabled for them to apply."},{"id":"app-ii2bg3","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A business needs a process that guides call-centre agents through a series of screens, collects answers, and creates a case. Which Flow type is right?","o":["Record-triggered flow","Scheduled-triggered flow","Screen flow","Platform event-triggered flow"],"a":[2],"e":"Screen flows provide a user interface with screens and fields, so they suit guided processes started by a user."},{"id":"app-g19lz6","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A flow should update a field on the record that triggered it as quickly as possible, with no additional DML. Which configuration should be used?","o":["A record-triggered flow that runs before the record is saved","A record-triggered flow that runs after the record is saved","A scheduled-triggered flow","An autolaunched flow"],"a":[0],"e":"Before-save flows update fields on the triggering record directly, without a separate update, so they are faster. They cannot be used to create or update other records."},{"id":"app-2u4qyt","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A flow updates a related record inside a loop element, once for each item. What is the best practice?","o":["Keep the update inside the loop.","Add each record to a collection inside the loop, then update the collection once after the loop.","Replace the loop with a validation rule.","Move the loop into a formula field."],"a":[1],"e":"Putting DML (create, update, delete) or queries inside a loop can hit governor limits when many records are processed. Collect records in a collection and run the operation once outside the loop."},{"id":"app-2z97sp","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A process requires a manager to approve a discount, then a finance reviewer for amounts above a threshold, with multiple steps and different users. Which Salesforce capability is designed for multi-step, multi-user work with approvals?","o":["A validation rule chain","Flow Orchestration or flow-based approval processes","A formula field","A report subscription"],"a":[1],"e":"Flow Orchestrator coordinates multi-step, multi-user processes made of stages and steps, including approvals and screen flows for different users."},{"id":"app-1ygejcm","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A flow was edited and the new version breaks a process. What is the quickest way to restore the previous behaviour?","o":["Delete the flow.","Activate the previous version of the flow.","Restore the flow from the Recycle Bin.","Create a new org."],"a":[1],"e":"A flow can have multiple versions but only one active version. Activating an earlier version rolls back to the earlier logic."},{"id":"app-ufdo96","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A record-triggered flow sometimes fails when updating an account. The business wants failures to create a log record and notify the admin. What should the app builder add?","o":["A validation rule.","A fault path on the element that can fail.","A bigger screen.","A formula field."],"a":[1],"e":"Fault connectors route the flow to error handling when an element fails, where you can log details and notify someone, instead of showing a generic error."},{"id":"app-d73mhy","d":"logic","m":true,"q":"Which TWO tools help an app builder find out why a flow is failing? (Choose 2)","o":["The Debug option in Flow Builder","A custom report type","Failed Flow Interviews and flow error emails","The AppExchange"],"a":[0,2],"e":"Debug runs the flow with test inputs and shows the path and values. Error emails and the paused and failed interview list show runtime failures in production."},{"id":"app-hyv1r6","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A flow should run only when the Amount changes from below 10,000 to 10,000 or more, not every time the record is saved. Which setting helps?","o":["The \"only when a record is updated to meet the condition requirements\" option in the entry criteria","A scheduled path","An approval process","A page layout"],"a":[0],"e":"Setting the flow to run only when the record is updated to meet the conditions prevents it from running again on every save when the condition was already true."},{"id":"app-ze1836","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A team wants an AI agent to look up an order status and issue a refund using actions that already exist as flows. What lets the agent do that?","o":["Adding the flows as actions for the agent's topics","Making the flow a validation rule","Putting the flow on a page layout","Assigning the flow a record type"],"a":[0],"e":"Agentforce agents use topics and actions, and flows can be added as actions so the agent can perform tasks."},{"id":"app-16gd1i0","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"The same set of steps (create audit record, notify owner) is needed in five different flows. What is the best way to build it?","o":["Build a subflow once and call it from each flow.","Copy and paste the elements into each flow.","Use five formula fields.","Create five validation rules."],"a":[0],"e":"Subflows let you reuse logic, so a change is made in one place."},{"id":"app-5q9ed2","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"Different sales teams need different layouts of the Account record page, with some components shown only to the Enterprise team. What should the app builder use?","o":["Multiple profiles with the same page layout.","Lightning record pages with different assignments, and component visibility filters","Several record types with the same page.","A custom object per team."],"a":[1],"e":"Lightning App Builder lets you create record pages and assign them by app, record type and profile, and component visibility rules show elements only under specific conditions."},{"id":"app-es47oy","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"Rather than managing one big page layout, the team wants to place individual fields on a Lightning record page and show them only when certain conditions are met. Which feature provides this?","o":["Compact layouts","Page layout field-level security","Dynamic Forms","Related lists"],"a":[2],"e":"Dynamic Forms let you place fields and sections directly on the Lightning page with visibility rules, which reduces the number of page layouts you maintain."},{"id":"app-he701r","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A button should appear on a record page only when the Status is Open. Which feature supports this?","o":["Page layout button section","Dynamic Actions","A validation rule","A global action"],"a":[1],"e":"Dynamic Actions let you control which actions appear, with filters based on record fields and user criteria."},{"id":"app-35sry9","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A user wants a button on Opportunity that launches a flow asking for details and creating a task. What should be configured?","o":["A quick action (a flow action) added to the page","A custom report type","A new profile","A validation rule"],"a":[0],"e":"Quick actions can launch flows, and you can add them to the page layout or Lightning page."},{"id":"app-1xai8bx","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"Which setting controls which fields appear in the highlights area at the top of a record in Lightning Experience and in the mobile app?","o":["Page layouts only","Field-level security","Compact layouts","Record types"],"a":[2],"e":"Compact layouts determine the key fields shown in the highlights panel and in the mobile app record header and cards."},{"id":"app-1352ra1","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A button must open an external company site, passing the current account's name in the URL. What should the app builder use?","o":["A custom button or link of type URL with merge fields","A roll-up summary field","A validation rule","A page layout section"],"a":[0],"e":"Custom links and buttons can open URLs and use merge fields to pass record data."},{"id":"app-eon8v6","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A team needs a highly interactive component with custom behaviour not available in standard components. What should the app builder recommend?","o":["A custom Lightning web component built by a developer, added to the page in Lightning App Builder","A bigger page layout","Another report","A custom field"],"a":[0],"e":"Custom Lightning web components extend the UI where standard components cannot, and the app builder can place them on a page declaratively once built."},{"id":"app-mx1apb","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"Service agents work with many cases at once and need multiple tabs and a utility bar with Omni-Channel. Which type of Lightning app should be used?","o":["Standard navigation app","Console navigation app","A mobile-only app","A Visualforce app"],"a":[1],"e":"Console navigation apps let users work with several records in tabs and subtabs, with utilities like Omni-Channel and history in the footer."},{"id":"app-16n4rmr","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A mobile user wants to quickly log a call from the Salesforce mobile app. What helps most?","o":["Quick actions in the mobile-optimised actions list","A new report type","A larger dashboard","A validation rule"],"a":[0],"e":"Quick actions placed at the top of the action list make common tasks fast on mobile."},{"id":"app-d86m03","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A global action versus an object-specific action: which statement is correct?","o":["A global action can be used anywhere without a related record, such as logging a call, while an object-specific action is tied to a particular object and automatically relates new records.","A global action is available only on Account.","An object-specific action can be used on all objects.","They are the same thing."],"a":[0],"e":"Global actions are not tied to a specific object record, and object-specific actions are associated with an object, which allows them to relate records and prefill fields."},{"id":"app-1ecx9sk","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A company wants to add a Visualforce page to a record page without code changes. How is this done?","o":["Add the Visualforce component to the Lightning record page in Lightning App Builder","Add it as a new field","Add it as a profile setting","Add it to a report"],"a":[0],"e":"Lightning App Builder offers a Visualforce component that displays a page on a Lightning page."},{"id":"app-1gi0z08","d":"deploy","m":false,"q":"A team needs a sandbox containing a full copy of production data and metadata for performance testing. Which sandbox type is needed?","o":["Developer","Developer Pro","Partial Copy","Full"],"a":[3],"e":"A full sandbox copies all production data and metadata, so it suits performance and load testing. Partial Copy sandboxes contain a sample of data."},{"id":"app-fu72n5","d":"deploy","m":false,"q":"A team needs a quick, cheap sandbox that contains only metadata for building a new feature. Which type is best?","o":["Developer sandbox","Full sandbox","Production","Partial Copy sandbox"],"a":[0],"e":"Developer sandboxes copy metadata only, with a small amount of storage, and are intended for development and testing by individual developers or admins."},{"id":"app-1y1egs5","d":"deploy","m":true,"q":"Which TWO statements about change sets are true? (Choose 2)","o":["Change sets move metadata between related orgs, such as a sandbox and production, over a deployment connection.","Change sets can be used to deploy between any two unrelated orgs.","Change sets do not support every type of metadata.","Change sets automatically delete components in the target org."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Change sets work between orgs that are connected (for example a production org and its sandboxes), and not all components are supported, so some settings need manual setup. They cannot delete components."},{"id":"app-1cdu7yd","d":"deploy","m":false,"q":"An app builder uploads an outbound change set to production, but production does not show it. What should be checked?","o":["The deployment connection and whether the target org has authorised uploads from the source org","The page layouts of the target org","The record types in the source org","The Chatter feed"],"a":[0],"e":"Change sets are sent over a deployment connection. The target org must allow inbound changes from the sandbox."},{"id":"app-6cimzv","d":"deploy","m":false,"q":"A deployment of a change set fails because a field used by a component is missing in the target org. What is the best fix?","o":["Use View/Add Dependencies to add the missing component to the change set and deploy again.","Delete the change set.","Retry the deploy until it works.","Change the profile of the user."],"a":[0],"e":"Dependency checks show components that a selected component needs. Adding the dependencies ensures everything required exists in the target org."},{"id":"app-1nnno7c","d":"deploy","m":false,"q":"The business wants to distribute a solution to many customer orgs, and wants to be able to push upgrades later. Which package type fits?","o":["Unmanaged package","Managed package","A change set","A sandbox"],"a":[1],"e":"Managed packages support versioning and upgrades, which is why ISVs use them to distribute apps. Unmanaged packages are a one-time copy."},{"id":"app-1okw2z","d":"deploy","m":false,"q":"A team wants to test business-user acceptance with realistic data but does not need all production data. Which sandbox is the most appropriate and cost-efficient?","o":["Partial Copy sandbox","Developer sandbox with no data","A scratch org","Production"],"a":[0],"e":"Partial Copy sandboxes contain metadata and a sample of production data defined by a template, which suits user acceptance testing."},{"id":"app-qlrbhv","d":"deploy","m":false,"q":"When a sandbox is refreshed, what happens to the work in progress in that sandbox?","o":["It is replaced by the current production metadata, so unfinished changes must be saved elsewhere first.","It is merged with production.","It is kept and production is updated.","Nothing changes."],"a":[0],"e":"A refresh recreates the sandbox from production, overwriting the sandbox's content, so unsaved work, for example changes not yet deployed, is lost."}]},"pd1":{"id":"pd1","short":"Platform Developer I","name":"Salesforce Certified Platform Developer I","blurb":"Developer fundamentals, Apex and automation logic, user interfaces and LWC, testing and deployment.","exam":{"questions":60,"unscored":"up to 5 unscored","minutes":105,"passing":68,"fee":"US$200 (retake US$100)","release":"Summer '25","guide":"https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=005298965&language=en_US&type=1","trailhead":"https://trailhead.salesforce.com/credentials/platformdeveloperi"},"domains":[{"n":16,"id":"fundamentals","name":"Developer Fundamentals","pct":27},{"n":17,"id":"logic","name":"Process Automation and Logic","pct":28},{"n":16,"id":"ui","name":"User Interface","pct":25},{"n":13,"id":"testing","name":"Testing, Debugging, and Deployment","pct":20}],"questions":[{"id":"pd1-1g0t316","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"Why does Salesforce enforce governor limits on Apex code?","o":["To make debugging easier for developers.","Because many customers share the same infrastructure (multi-tenancy), so limits stop one customer's code from using too many shared resources.","To force developers to use Visualforce.","To keep the number of triggers per object low."],"a":[1],"e":"Salesforce is a multi-tenant platform. Governor limits protect shared resources such as CPU, memory and database capacity so that one org's code cannot degrade performance for the others."},{"id":"pd1-16pngn0","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"In the MVC pattern as it applies on the Salesforce platform, which part represents the Model?","o":["Lightning web components","Apex controllers","Objects, fields and relationships (the data model)","Visualforce pages"],"a":[2],"e":"The model is the data layer: standard and custom objects with their fields and relationships. Views are pages and components, and controllers are the logic, such as Apex classes and flows."},{"id":"pd1-2fi2ds","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"A requirement is to set a field on the parent account whenever a child record meets simple criteria. A developer is considering a trigger. What should the developer consider first?","o":["Apex is always faster to maintain.","Whether declarative tools such as a record-triggered flow can meet the requirement, since they are easier for admins to maintain.","Whether the code can be written in a single class.","Whether the org uses Visualforce."],"a":[1],"e":"A common best practice is to use declarative features where they meet the need and to use code when requirements go beyond what they can do."},{"id":"pd1-1ur4okv","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"What is the maximum number of SOQL queries allowed in a single synchronous Apex transaction?","o":["50","100","150","200"],"a":[1],"e":"Synchronous Apex transactions are limited to 100 SOQL queries (200 in asynchronous contexts). Exceeding the limit throws an uncatchable exception."},{"id":"pd1-pc2nya","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"What is the maximum number of records that can be processed by DML statements in one Apex transaction?","o":["150","2,000","50,000","10,000"],"a":[3],"e":"A transaction can process up to 10,000 records through DML. There is also a limit of 150 DML statements."},{"id":"pd1-gftok","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"A developer wraps a section of code in try/catch and the transaction exceeds a governor limit. What happens?","o":["The catch block handles the error and the code continues.","The limit exception cannot be caught, so the transaction is terminated.","The limit is automatically increased.","The next transaction starts automatically."],"a":[1],"e":"Governor limit exceptions (System.LimitException) cannot be caught. Developers must design the code to stay within the limits."},{"id":"pd1-1cy5cji","d":"fundamentals","m":true,"q":"Which TWO statements correctly describe formula fields and roll-up summary fields compared with writing Apex? (Choose 2)","o":["A formula field is calculated when the record is viewed and needs no code or tests.","A roll-up summary field can be created on any lookup relationship.","A roll-up summary field summarises child records on the master of a master-detail relationship.","A formula field stores its value permanently in the database."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Formula fields calculate their value when displayed and roll-up summary fields aggregate child data on the master side of master-detail relationships. Using them avoids code for simple needs."},{"id":"pd1-1xa097y","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"A developer needs to query all contacts for each account in a single query. Which SOQL is correct?","o":["SELECT Id, Contacts FROM Account","SELECT Id, (SELECT Id FROM Contacts) FROM Account","SELECT Id, Account.Contacts FROM Contact","SELECT Id FROM Account JOIN Contact"],"a":[1],"e":"A parent-to-child subquery uses the child relationship name, which for contacts on an account is Contacts. SOQL does not support JOIN syntax."},{"id":"pd1-1yrgr1s","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"What is the correct way to reference the account name from a contact in SOQL?","o":["SELECT Name.Account FROM Contact","SELECT Account.Name FROM Contact","SELECT Contact.Account.Name FROM Account","SELECT AccountName FROM Contact"],"a":[1],"e":"Child-to-parent queries use dot notation through the relationship field, such as Account.Name."},{"id":"pd1-1nfta2l","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"A custom lookup field named Region__c on an object points to a custom object. How is the related record's name referenced in SOQL on the child?","o":["Region__c.Name","Region__r.Name","Region__c__r.Name","Region.Name__c"],"a":[1],"e":"For custom relationships, the relationship name replaces __c with __r when traversing to the parent's fields."},{"id":"pd1-1nc3v1i","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"A developer wants to insert or update records using an ID from an external system, without first querying for Salesforce IDs. What should be used?","o":["upsert with an External ID field","insert only","delete then insert","merge"],"a":[0],"e":"Upsert matches records using an External ID or the Salesforce ID, inserting new records and updating existing ones in one operation."},{"id":"pd1-1wb1g2m","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"Which framework is recommended for building new custom user interface components on the Salesforce platform?","o":["Aura components","Lightning Web Components","Visualforce","Apex-only controllers"],"a":[1],"e":"Lightning Web Components are built on modern web standards and are the recommended choice for new Lightning UI development."},{"id":"pd1-12zzb2b","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"A developer wants application configuration records that are deployed between orgs together with the code, instead of being re-entered by hand in each org. Which option fits?","o":["A hierarchy custom setting","Custom metadata types","A custom label","A list of static strings in a class"],"a":[1],"e":"Custom metadata type records are metadata, so they can be deployed and packaged with the code. Custom settings records are data, which are not deployed with the metadata."},{"id":"pd1-1eb06ed","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"Which is a recommended use of an AI coding assistant such as Agentforce for developers?","o":["Generating draft code or tests that the developer then reviews, tests and edits before using.","Deploying code to production without review.","Replacing the need for a sandbox.","Granting permissions to users."],"a":[0],"e":"AI assistants can speed up drafting code and explanations, but the developer remains responsible for reviewing, testing and securing the result, and for not sharing sensitive data."},{"id":"pd1-ngmfhq","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"Why is it a best practice not to hard-code record IDs in Apex?","o":["IDs differ between orgs and sandboxes, so hard-coded IDs break when code is deployed.","IDs are always the same in all orgs.","Hard-coded IDs are slower.","Salesforce blocks IDs in strings."],"a":[0],"e":"Record IDs are specific to each org. Query by a stable value such as a developer name, or use configuration, so the code works after deployment and sandbox refreshes."},{"id":"pd1-1kjeqas","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"In Apex, what happens when an Id variable holding a record's 15-character Id is compared with == to the 18-character Id of the same record?","o":["They are never equal.","They are equal, because Apex treats both forms of the Id as the same record.","The code throws a type exception.","Only the first 3 characters are compared."],"a":[1],"e":"The 18-character Id adds a case-safe suffix to the 15-character form. Apex Id values compare equal for the same record in either form, though 18 characters is the safer form to store and share."},{"id":"pd1-5vsgk","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"Which declaration creates a constant in Apex?","o":["static Integer MAX = 5;","static final Integer MAX = 5;","const Integer MAX = 5;","private Integer MAX = 5;"],"a":[1],"e":"The final keyword makes a variable's value assignable only once. A constant is usually declared static final."},{"id":"pd1-95qtdf","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A class implements an interface that declares two methods but the class defines only one of them. What happens?","o":["The class compiles and the missing method returns null.","A compile error, because a class that implements an interface must implement all its methods.","The class runs but the method is skipped.","The missing method is added automatically."],"a":[1],"e":"A non-abstract class must provide an implementation for every method in the interfaces it implements."},{"id":"pd1-1okzl5z","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"Which access modifier allows a method to be called only from inside the class where it is defined?","o":["global","public","protected","private"],"a":[3],"e":"Private members are visible only within the defining class (and its inner classes). Protected extends visibility to subclasses."},{"id":"pd1-1m1u2rk","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"Given the following code, what is the result when no account is named Acme?\n```\nAccount a = [SELECT Id FROM Account WHERE Name = 'Acme'];\n```","o":["a is an empty Account.","a is null and no error occurs.","A QueryException is thrown, because assigning a query to a single record requires exactly one result.","A DmlException is thrown."],"a":[2],"e":"When a SOQL query assigned to a single sObject returns no rows (or more than one), Apex throws a QueryException. Assign to a List to handle zero or many rows safely."},{"id":"pd1-1tt8uoy","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"What type does a SOSL query return in Apex?","o":["A list of sObjects","A map of Id to sObject","A list of lists of sObjects","A single sObject"],"a":[2],"e":"SOSL searches across several objects, so it returns a list of lists, one list per object returned in the query."},{"id":"pd1-193pet","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A developer wants to update 200 accounts and continue processing even if some records fail validation. Which statement enables partial success?","o":["update accounts;","Database.update(accounts, false);","Database.update(accounts, true);","insert accounts;"],"a":[1],"e":"With the Database methods, setting allOrNone to false lets valid records succeed and returns results for the failures. The update statement fails the whole operation when any record fails."},{"id":"pd1-1gebczd","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"The following trigger runs when 200 accounts are inserted. What is the problem?\n```\ntrigger AccountTrigger on Account (after insert) {\n    for (Account a : Trigger.new) {\n        Contact c = [SELECT Id FROM Contact WHERE AccountId = :a.Id LIMIT 1];\n    }\n}\n```","o":["Trigger.new cannot be used in an after insert trigger.","A SOQL query is inside a loop, so 200 records exceed the 100 query limit.","The LIMIT clause is not allowed in triggers.","Triggers cannot query contacts."],"a":[1],"e":"Queries (and DML) inside loops are not bulk-safe. Collect the IDs first, run one query with an IN clause, and use a map."},{"id":"pd1-1lti14r","d":"logic","m":true,"q":"Which TWO are Apex trigger best practices? (Choose 2)","o":["Have one trigger per object and keep logic in handler classes.","Query and update inside for loops for simplicity.","Write code that handles collections of records, not just one record.","Hard-code record IDs in the trigger."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Bulkification, one trigger per object and logic-less triggers make behaviour predictable and testable."},{"id":"pd1-um6b3n","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"In which trigger event is Trigger.old not available?","o":["before insert","before update","before delete","after update"],"a":[0],"e":"Trigger.old holds the previous versions of records and exists only for update and delete events. Nothing existed before an insert."},{"id":"pd1-1ok392z","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A developer needs to set a field on records being inserted without an additional DML statement. Which context should be used?","o":["before insert","after insert","after update","before delete"],"a":[0],"e":"In before triggers the records in Trigger.new can be modified directly, and the changes are saved with the record without an extra update."},{"id":"pd1-14w2iyl","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A trigger updates a field on an account, which fires an update trigger that updates the account again, repeatedly. What is the standard way to stop this?","o":["Use a static variable (for example a Set of processed IDs) to control re-entry.","Add more triggers.","Replace the trigger with a formula.","Use a future method inside the loop."],"a":[0],"e":"Static variables keep their value for the duration of a transaction, so they can be used to make sure logic runs only once per record."},{"id":"pd1-1soyjx2","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"Which scenario throws a MixedDmlException?","o":["Inserting an account and a contact in the same transaction.","Inserting an account and then a user (a setup object) in the same transaction.","Updating two accounts in a loop.","Calling a callout before a DML statement."],"a":[1],"e":"Setup objects such as User and non-setup objects such as Account cannot be changed in the same transaction. Separate them, for example with asynchronous Apex."},{"id":"pd1-7is7rm","d":"logic","m":true,"q":"Which TWO statements about custom exceptions in Apex are true? (Choose 2)","o":["A custom exception class must extend Exception and its name must end with \"Exception\".","A custom exception can only be thrown, never caught.","A custom exception can be thrown with throw new MyException('message');","Custom exceptions are not allowed in triggers."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Define the class with extends Exception and a name that ends with Exception, then throw and catch it like built-in exceptions."},{"id":"pd1-1imaz3p","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A flow needs to call Apex code that sends an email to a customer. What must the Apex method have to be callable from a flow?","o":["The @InvocableMethod annotation, on a static method that accepts a list","The @future annotation","The @isTest annotation","The global keyword on every method"],"a":[0],"e":"Invocable methods are exposed to flows and agent actions. They must be static, and take (and often return) a list so they can handle many inputs at once."},{"id":"pd1-1e6vqfq","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A developer needs a collection of unique account IDs from a list of contacts. Which collection fits best?","o":["List<Id>","Set<Id>","Map<Id, Contact>","Integer[]"],"a":[1],"e":"A Set holds unique values, so duplicate IDs are removed automatically, which also helps when binding them in a query."},{"id":"pd1-1yeo8pi","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"How can a developer quickly build a map of accounts keyed by Id from a query?","o":["Map<Id, Account> m = new Map<Id, Account>([SELECT Id, Name FROM Account]);","Map<Id, Account> m = [SELECT Id FROM Account].toMap();","Map<Id, Account> m = new Map<Id>();","Map<Id, Account> m = Account.getMap();"],"a":[0],"e":"The Map constructor accepts a list of sObjects and uses each record's Id as the key."},{"id":"pd1-r751a6","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A transaction inserts several records, then an uncaught exception is thrown at the end. What happens to the earlier DML in that transaction?","o":["It is rolled back, because an unhandled exception undoes the entire transaction.","It is kept in the database.","It is committed in the background.","It is committed for the first 50 records only."],"a":[0],"e":"Apex transactions are all or nothing: if the transaction ends with an unhandled error, all the changes made in it are rolled back."},{"id":"pd1-1cozhuc","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"What does the with sharing keyword do on an Apex class?","o":["It lets the class ignore field-level security.","It makes the class respect the running user's record-level sharing rules.","It shares the class with other orgs.","It runs the class in a new transaction."],"a":[1],"e":"By default Apex runs in system context. with sharing enforces the user's sharing rules (record access) for queries inside the class, but not object or field permissions."},{"id":"pd1-18b8etd","d":"ui","m":true,"q":"A developer must make sure queried data respects the user's object and field permissions. Which options help? (Choose 2)","o":["Add WITH USER_MODE to the SOQL query.","Mark the class global.","Use Security.stripInaccessible() on query results.","Add the without sharing keyword."],"a":[0,2],"e":"User mode and stripInaccessible apply object and field-level security, which Apex does not enforce by default in system mode."},{"id":"pd1-1wlbyhj","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A search page builds a query by concatenating user input into a dynamic SOQL string. What is the best way to prevent SOQL injection?","o":["Use a bigger LIMIT clause.","Use bind variables, or escape input with String.escapeSingleQuotes if concatenation is unavoidable.","Run the code without sharing.","Convert the string to uppercase."],"a":[1],"e":"Bind variables treat input as data rather than query text. Escaping single quotes helps when building dynamic strings."},{"id":"pd1-9oag95","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A Visualforce page displays text entered by users. Which setting helps protect against cross-site scripting?","o":["Setting escape=\"false\" on output components.","Keeping the default HTML encoding on merge fields and output components.","Moving the page to production only.","Using JavaScript alerts."],"a":[1],"e":"Visualforce HTML-encodes merge fields by default. Disabling the escaping can allow user-supplied scripts to run."},{"id":"pd1-xw0y1m","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"In a Lightning web component, how does a parent set a value in a child component?","o":["By dispatching a custom event from the parent.","By assigning a value to a public property decorated with @api in the child.","By calling an Apex method.","By writing to the DOM of the child directly."],"a":[1],"e":"Public properties and methods are exposed with @api. Parents pass data down through attributes in the template."},{"id":"pd1-1jvpxz8","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"How does a child Lightning web component send information to its parent?","o":["By changing the parent's properties.","By using @wire on the parent.","By dispatching a CustomEvent that the parent handles.","By using a global variable."],"a":[2],"e":"Child components fire custom events and parents listen for them, which keeps data flowing down through properties and events flowing up."},{"id":"pd1-orjjxo","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A Lightning web component should load data from Apex when it renders and refresh it when a parameter changes. Which approach is best?","o":["Wire an Apex method that is annotated with @AuraEnabled(cacheable=true).","Call the Apex method in the constructor with setTimeout.","Use a Visualforce page.","Use an SOQL query in the HTML template."],"a":[0],"e":"The @wire service provisions data reactively, and Apex methods used with it must be cacheable, meaning they must not perform DML."},{"id":"pd1-zfzxfn","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A Lightning web component must save a record through Apex when the user clicks a button. How should the Apex method be exposed?","o":["With @AuraEnabled(cacheable=true), called with @wire","With @AuraEnabled (not cacheable), called imperatively","With @future","With @isTest"],"a":[1],"e":"Methods that change data cannot be cacheable. Call them imperatively from the event handler."},{"id":"pd1-44jnj1","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"Which lifecycle hook runs when a Lightning web component is inserted into the DOM?","o":["disconnectedCallback","connectedCallback","renderedCallback only","errorCallback"],"a":[1],"e":"connectedCallback fires when the component is inserted into the DOM. It is a good place to start loading data."},{"id":"pd1-xadomy","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A page must produce a PDF invoice. Which technology is best suited?","o":["A Lightning web component.","A Visualforce page with renderAs=\"pdf\".","A validation rule.","A roll-up summary field."],"a":[1],"e":"Visualforce can render pages as PDF, which is why it is still used for documents such as invoices."},{"id":"pd1-10t7izd","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A developer needs to display and edit a record's fields in a Lightning web component without writing Apex. What should be used?","o":["lightning-record-form or Lightning Data Service wire adapters","A trigger","A batch job","A scheduled flow"],"a":[0],"e":"Lightning Data Service and the base components built on it handle data access, security and caching without Apex."},{"id":"pd1-monvn2","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A custom Lightning web component needs to appear as a screen inside a flow. Which target must the component's metadata include?","o":["lightning__RecordPage","lightning__FlowScreen","lightning__HomePage","lightning__Tab"],"a":[1],"e":"Components exposed to flows declare the lightning__FlowScreen target (and can use properties as flow inputs and outputs)."},{"id":"pd1-1hz9f2w","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A developer wants to show a toast message after a record is saved in a Lightning web component. Which approach is correct?","o":["Dispatch a ShowToastEvent","Use alert() only","Use a validation rule","Use a roll-up summary field"],"a":[0],"e":"The ShowToastEvent from lightning/platformShowToastEvent displays toast messages in Lightning Experience."},{"id":"pd1-15utfbz","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A developer exposes an Apex method as an action that an Agentforce agent can run. What is typically required?","o":["An invocable method (or flow) registered as an action for the agent","A Visualforce page","A custom report type","A trigger on User"],"a":[0],"e":"Agents run actions, and Apex can be exposed to them through invocable methods that are added as agent actions."},{"id":"pd1-15huymw","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"When is it preferable to use a Lightning web component instead of Aura for a new component?","o":["Almost always for new development, because LWC is based on web standards and is the recommended framework.","Never, because LWC cannot call Apex.","Only when the page is for mobile.","Only in Salesforce Classic."],"a":[0],"e":"Aura still works and is supported, but new components are recommended to be built as Lightning web components."},{"id":"pd1-17gj4bl","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"Which method is used to navigate from a Lightning web component to a record page?","o":["window.location.href only","NavigationMixin with a page reference","An Apex redirect","A validation rule"],"a":[1],"e":"The NavigationMixin generates and follows page references so navigation works across Lightning Experience and the mobile app."},{"id":"pd1-1tyeiup","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"What is the minimum overall Apex code coverage required to deploy code to production?","o":["50%","65%","75%","100%"],"a":[2],"e":"At least 75% of Apex code must be covered by tests, and all tests must pass. Each trigger also needs some coverage."},{"id":"pd1-mzoztc","d":"testing","m":true,"q":"Which TWO practices apply when writing Apex tests? (Choose 2)","o":["Create the test data inside the test (or in @testSetup) instead of relying on existing org data.","Use @isTest(SeeAllData=true) on every class.","Assert the expected results with System.assertEquals or the Assert class.","Test only the positive scenario."],"a":[0,2],"e":"Tests should create their own data, check results with assertions, and cover positive, negative and bulk cases."},{"id":"pd1-1fduimb","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"What does Test.startTest() do?","o":["It starts a fresh set of governor limits for the code under test.","It starts the debug log.","It deploys the code.","It disables triggers."],"a":[0],"e":"Test.startTest() and Test.stopTest() mark the code under test and give it its own governor limits. Asynchronous work started inside completes at stopTest."},{"id":"pd1-1cbxsxg","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"What is the benefit of a method annotated with @testSetup?","o":["It creates test data once, and each test method in the class sees that data in its original state.","It runs after each test method.","It lets the test see all org data.","It disables sharing rules."],"a":[0],"e":"@testSetup runs once per class, and changes made by a test method are rolled back, so the next test sees the original setup data."},{"id":"pd1-1lhmj70","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"A test must verify behaviour for a user with a specific profile. Which method should be used?","o":["System.runAs(user)","System.debug(user)","Test.setCurrentUser","UserInfo.setProfile"],"a":[0],"e":"System.runAs runs a block of code as a given user, applying that user's record sharing (and some permissions), which is how tests verify user-specific behaviour."},{"id":"pd1-17g1l7z","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"Tests cannot make real HTTP callouts. What allows a test to simulate a response?","o":["Running the test with SeeAllData","Implementing HttpCalloutMock and calling Test.setMock","Using a future method","Adding a remote site setting only"],"a":[1],"e":"A mock class returns a fake response when the code makes a callout, so tests stay fast and independent of external systems."},{"id":"pd1-jkyg50","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"A developer wants to see the SOQL queries, DML and limit usage that happen when a user saves a record in a sandbox. Which tool should be used?","o":["Debug logs (set up with a trace flag), viewed in Developer Console or Setup","The Setup Audit Trail","The Data Import Wizard","Schema Builder"],"a":[0],"e":"Debug logs record detailed execution, including database operations and cumulative limits, and a trace flag defines which user and log levels are captured."},{"id":"pd1-1vuyqce","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"A developer wants to run asynchronous Apex jobs and check whether a batch finished or failed. Where can this be monitored?","o":["Apex Jobs in Setup","Field History Tracking","The AppExchange","Report types"],"a":[0],"e":"The Apex Jobs page shows the status of batch, future and queueable jobs, including errors."},{"id":"pd1-tx04u5","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"Which tool lets developers retrieve and deploy metadata and run tests from the command line in a source-driven workflow?","o":["The Data Import Wizard","Salesforce CLI","Schema Builder","Report Builder"],"a":[1],"e":"The Salesforce CLI works with Salesforce DX projects to create orgs, retrieve and deploy source, and run tests, and it fits into CI/CD."},{"id":"pd1-18pbq7s","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"When deploying Apex to production, which statement is true about running tests?","o":["By default all local tests run, and the org needs at least 75% overall coverage.","No tests run if the deployment is made by an admin.","Only managed package tests run.","Tests run only in sandboxes."],"a":[0],"e":"A deployment that includes Apex to production runs local tests by default. Validation-only deployments can check tests ahead of time."},{"id":"pd1-gi2uhy","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"A developer needs an isolated, disposable org created from a definition file for source-driven development. Which should be used?","o":["A full sandbox","A scratch org","Production","A change set"],"a":[1],"e":"Scratch orgs are temporary orgs configured from a definition file, designed for development and automated testing in a source-driven workflow."},{"id":"pd1-1bjdhhh","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"A team wants to verify an automated flow works as designed before activating it, using sample records and checking results. What can they use?","o":["Flow tests (and the debug option) in Flow Builder","Apex tests only","The Setup Audit Trail","Dashboards"],"a":[0],"e":"Flow Builder supports flow tests, which set up conditions, run the flow, and check outcomes, in addition to the debug tool."},{"id":"pd1-gpgjki","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"A developer tests code that behaves differently for 1 record and for 200 records. Which test approach is best?","o":["Add test methods that insert one record and test methods that insert a bulk list of 200 records.","Test only one record.","Use SeeAllData=true.","Use only System.debug."],"a":[0],"e":"Bulk tests catch limit issues and loops that work for one record but fail at scale."}]},"jsdev":{"id":"jsdev","short":"JavaScript Developer","name":"Salesforce Certified JavaScript Developer","blurb":"Core JavaScript: variables and types, objects and classes, the browser, async code, Node.js and testing.","exam":{"questions":60,"unscored":"up to 5 unscored","minutes":105,"passing":65,"fee":"US$200 (retake US$100)","release":"Summer '22","guide":"https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=005298945&language=en_US&type=1","trailhead":"https://trailhead.salesforce.com/credentials/javascriptdeveloper"},"domains":[{"n":12,"id":"vars","name":"Variables, Types, and Collections","pct":23},{"n":11,"id":"objects","name":"Objects, Functions, and Classes","pct":25},{"n":8,"id":"browser","name":"Browser and Events","pct":17},{"n":4,"id":"debug","name":"Debugging and Error Handling","pct":7},{"n":6,"id":"async","name":"Asynchronous Programming","pct":13},{"n":4,"id":"server","name":"Server Side JavaScript","pct":8},{"n":4,"id":"testing","name":"Testing","pct":7}],"questions":[{"id":"jsd-69vdb8","d":"vars","m":false,"q":"What does this code log?\n```js\nconsole.log(typeof null, typeof undefined, typeof []);\n```","o":["object undefined object","null undefined array","object undefined array","null object object"],"a":[0],"e":"typeof null returns \"object\", a long-standing quirk of the language. typeof undefined is \"undefined\", and arrays are objects, so typeof [] is also \"object\". Use Array.isArray() to tell an array from a plain object."},{"id":"jsd-1bjz5rk","d":"vars","m":false,"q":"What is the output?\n```js\nconsole.log(1 + '2', '3' - 1, '5' * '2');\n```","o":["12 2 10","3 2 10","12 31 52","3 2 52"],"a":[0],"e":"The + operator concatenates when either operand is a string, so 1 + '2' is '12'. The - and * operators always convert operands to numbers, so '3' - 1 is 2 and '5' * '2' is 10."},{"id":"jsd-1qe2kq","d":"vars","m":true,"q":"Which TWO values are falsy in JavaScript? (Choose 2)","o":["0","NaN","\"0\"","[]","{}"],"a":[0,1],"e":"The falsy values are false, 0, -0, 0n, \"\", null, undefined and NaN. The string \"0\", an empty array and an empty object are all objects or non-empty strings, so they are truthy."},{"id":"jsd-lsllf7","d":"vars","m":false,"q":"A developer needs a variable that must never be reassigned and is only visible inside the block where it is declared. Which declaration should they use?","o":["const","var","let","global"],"a":[0],"e":"const creates a block-scoped binding that cannot be reassigned. var is function-scoped, let is block-scoped but can be reassigned, and there is no global keyword for declarations."},{"id":"jsd-15ua4v8","d":"vars","m":false,"q":"What does this code log?\n```js\nconsole.log(a);\nvar a = 5;\n```","o":["undefined","5","It throws a ReferenceError","null"],"a":[0],"e":"Declarations made with var are hoisted to the top of their scope and initialised to undefined, but the assignment stays where it is. The log therefore prints undefined. With let or const the same code would throw a ReferenceError because of the temporal dead zone."},{"id":"jsd-pqyf6","d":"vars","m":false,"q":"What is the result of this comparison?\n```js\nconsole.log(0 == '', 0 === '', null == undefined, null === undefined);\n```","o":["true false true false","true true true false","false false true false","true false false false"],"a":[0],"e":"The loose == operator coerces types, so 0 == '' is true and null == undefined is true by a special rule. The strict === operator performs no coercion, so both strict comparisons are false."},{"id":"jsd-1re1c2l","d":"vars","m":false,"q":"A developer has an array of order totals and needs a new array containing each total with tax added, without changing the original array. Which method fits best?","o":["map","forEach","filter","reduce"],"a":[0],"e":"map returns a new array with one transformed element for each input element and leaves the original untouched. forEach returns undefined, filter keeps or drops elements without transforming them, and reduce collapses an array to a single value."},{"id":"jsd-18br1ez","d":"vars","m":false,"q":"What does this code log?\n```js\nconst nums = [1, 2, 3, 4];\nconst result = nums.reduce((sum, n) => sum + n, 10);\nconsole.log(result);\n```","o":["20","10","15","24"],"a":[0],"e":"reduce starts with the initial value 10 and adds each element: 10 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 equals 20. Without the second argument the first element would be used as the starting value and the result would be 10."},{"id":"jsd-dcldj1","d":"vars","m":false,"q":"What is logged by this code?\n```js\nconst data = '{\"name\":\"Ada\",\"skills\":[\"js\",\"apex\"]}';\nconst obj = JSON.parse(data);\nconsole.log(obj.skills.length, typeof data);\n```","o":["2 string","2 object","4 string","undefined string"],"a":[0],"e":"JSON.parse turns the JSON text into an object whose skills array has two entries. The variable data still holds the original text, so typeof data is \"string\"."},{"id":"jsd-hnu63v","d":"vars","m":false,"q":"Which statement about the Date object is correct?","o":["Months are zero-based, so new Date(2025, 0, 15) is 15 January 2025.","Months are one-based, so new Date(2025, 0, 15) is invalid.","Date stores its value as a string in ISO format.","Date objects can only represent dates after 1 January 2000."],"a":[0],"e":"JavaScript months run from 0 for January to 11 for December. A Date internally stores milliseconds since the Unix epoch, which is a number, and it can represent dates both before and after 1970."},{"id":"jsd-h4iifd","d":"vars","m":false,"q":"What does this code log?\n```js\nconst a = [1, 2, 3];\nconst b = a;\nb.push(4);\nconsole.log(a.length);\n```","o":["4","3","1","undefined"],"a":[0],"e":"Arrays are objects and variables hold references to them. Assigning a to b copies the reference, not the array, so a push through b is visible through a. Use the spread operator or slice to make a real copy."},{"id":"jsd-klz064","d":"vars","m":false,"q":"Which expression creates a shallow copy of the object user with an extra property admin set to true?","o":["{ ...user, admin: true }","user.admin = true","Object.freeze(user)","user.clone({ admin: true })"],"a":[0],"e":"Object spread copies the own enumerable properties of user into a new object, and the later admin property is added or overrides an existing one. Assigning to user.admin mutates the original, freeze prevents changes, and plain objects have no clone method."},{"id":"jsd-z5qvbt","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"What is logged by this code?\n```js\nfunction outer() {\n  let count = 0;\n  return function () {\n    count++;\n    return count;\n  };\n}\nconst c = outer();\nc();\nconsole.log(c());\n```","o":["2","1","0","undefined"],"a":[0],"e":"The inner function closes over the count variable, so it keeps access to it after outer has returned. The first call raises it to 1 and the second call returns 2."},{"id":"jsd-1bcfvpu","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"What does this code log?\n```js\nconst person = {\n  name: 'Sam',\n  greet() { return this.name; },\n  later: () => this.name\n};\nconsole.log(person.greet(), person.later());\n```","o":["Sam undefined","Sam Sam","undefined undefined","It throws a TypeError"],"a":[0],"e":"A method called with dot notation gets the object as this. An arrow function does not have its own this and uses the surrounding scope, which in a module or browser script is not the person object, so this.name is undefined there."},{"id":"jsd-1d0u1xi","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"A developer writes a class and wants a subclass to reuse the parent constructor. What must the subclass constructor do before it uses this?","o":["Call super() with any arguments the parent needs","Call this.parent()","Call Object.create on the parent","Nothing, because this is set up automatically"],"a":[0],"e":"In a derived class the this binding does not exist until super() has run. Accessing this before calling super throws a ReferenceError."},{"id":"jsd-1j7ny1r","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"Which statement about the class keyword in JavaScript is correct?","o":["It is syntax built on top of prototypes and constructor functions.","It introduces a separate class-based object model that replaces prototypes.","Classes are hoisted and can be used before their declaration.","Class fields are always private."],"a":[0],"e":"Classes are mostly syntactic sugar over prototype-based inheritance. Class declarations are not usable before the declaration is evaluated, and fields are public unless they start with a hash character."},{"id":"jsd-v78510","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"What is the output?\n```js\nconst obj = { a: 1, b: { c: 2 } };\nconst copy = { ...obj };\ncopy.b.c = 99;\nconsole.log(obj.b.c);\n```","o":["99","2","undefined","It throws an error"],"a":[0],"e":"The spread operator makes a shallow copy. The nested object b is shared between obj and copy, so changing copy.b.c also changes obj.b.c. Use structuredClone for a deep copy."},{"id":"jsd-cxv5im","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"Which function call syntax lets a developer invoke greet with this set to the user object and pass the arguments as a list?","o":["greet.call(user, 'Hi', '!')","greet.bind(user, 'Hi', '!')","greet.apply(user, 'Hi', '!')","greet.this(user, 'Hi', '!')"],"a":[0],"e":"call invokes the function immediately with a chosen this and arguments listed individually. bind returns a new function without invoking it, and apply expects the arguments in a single array."},{"id":"jsd-engo5l","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"What does this module code do?\n```js\n// math.js\nexport const add = (a, b) => a + b;\nexport default function multiply(a, b) { return a * b; }\n```\nWhich import statement correctly loads both exports?","o":["import multiply, { add } from './math.js';","import { multiply, add } from './math.js';","import add, { multiply } from './math.js';","import * as multiply from './math.js';"],"a":[0],"e":"A default export is imported without braces and under any name, while named exports go inside braces and must match the exported names. So multiply is the default import and add is a named import."},{"id":"jsd-1rlcmgo","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"What does this code log?\n```js\nfunction test() {\n  if (true) {\n    var x = 1;\n    let y = 2;\n  }\n  console.log(typeof x, typeof y);\n}\ntest();\n```","o":["number undefined","number number","undefined undefined","undefined number"],"a":[0],"e":"var is function-scoped, so x is visible after the if block. let is block-scoped, so y does not exist outside the block, and typeof on an undeclared name returns \"undefined\" rather than throwing."},{"id":"jsd-sz6e1q","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"Which statement about prototypes is correct?","o":["If a property is not found on an object, JavaScript looks for it on the object's prototype chain.","Every object has its own copy of all properties from its prototype.","Prototypes can only be set when a class is declared.","Changing a prototype never affects objects that already exist."],"a":[0],"e":"Property lookup walks up the prototype chain until it finds the property or reaches null. Instances share the prototype rather than copying it, so adding a method to the prototype later is visible to existing instances."},{"id":"jsd-pp0btt","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"What is the output?\n```js\nconst fn = (a, b = 2, ...rest) => [a, b, rest.length];\nconsole.log(fn(1), fn(1, undefined, 3, 4));\n```","o":["[1,2,0] [1,2,2]","[1,undefined,0] [1,undefined,2]","[1,2,0] [1,3,1]","[1,2,undefined] [1,2,2]"],"a":[0],"e":"A default parameter is used when the argument is missing or undefined. In the second call b receives undefined and therefore falls back to 2, and the rest parameter collects the remaining arguments 3 and 4, so its length is 2."},{"id":"jsd-1ior9cu","d":"objects","m":false,"q":"Which statement about static class members is correct?","o":["A static method is called on the class itself, not on instances.","A static method can be called on any instance of the class.","Static properties are copied into every new instance.","Static methods can use this to read instance fields."],"a":[0],"e":"Static members belong to the class constructor. Instances do not have them, and inside a static method this refers to the class, not to an instance."},{"id":"jsd-ewy8wr","d":"browser","m":false,"q":"A user clicks a button inside a div that also has a click listener. Both elements have listeners that use the default settings. In which order do the handlers run?","o":["Button first, then the div","Div first, then the button","Only the button handler runs","Both run at the same time"],"a":[0],"e":"By default events bubble from the target element up through its ancestors, so the handler on the button runs before the handler on the div. Capturing handlers, which run top-down, only happen if capture is requested."},{"id":"jsd-1nyehhp","d":"browser","m":false,"q":"Which method stops an event from reaching the listeners of parent elements?","o":["event.stopPropagation()","event.preventDefault()","event.stopImmediate()","event.cancelBubble = false"],"a":[0],"e":"stopPropagation prevents the event from continuing along the propagation path. preventDefault only cancels the browser's default action, such as following a link or submitting a form."},{"id":"jsd-1ry03oz","d":"browser","m":false,"q":"A list has hundreds of items that are added and removed dynamically. How can the developer handle clicks on items efficiently?","o":["Attach one click listener to the parent list and check event.target","Attach a separate listener to every item each time one is added","Poll the list every second for changes","Replace the list with a canvas element"],"a":[0],"e":"Event delegation uses bubbling. One listener on the parent receives clicks from any current or future child, and event.target (or closest) tells it which item was clicked."},{"id":"jsd-xolky5","d":"browser","m":true,"q":"Which TWO statements about document.querySelectorAll are true? (Choose 2)","o":["It accepts a CSS selector string.","It returns a static NodeList that does not update when the page changes.","It returns a live HTMLCollection.","It can only find elements by id.","It returns a single element."],"a":[0,1],"e":"querySelectorAll takes any CSS selector and returns a static NodeList snapshot. Methods such as getElementsByClassName are the ones that return live HTMLCollections, and querySelector returns just the first match."},{"id":"jsd-pgdz4m","d":"browser","m":false,"q":"Which property should a developer prefer to insert untrusted user text into an element without risking script injection?","o":["textContent","innerHTML","outerHTML","insertAdjacentHTML"],"a":[0],"e":"textContent treats the value as plain text, so markup in it is not parsed. The HTML-based properties parse the string as markup and can run attacker-supplied elements or handlers."},{"id":"jsd-jb2fvv","d":"browser","m":false,"q":"A developer wants to store a small piece of data in the browser that survives closing and reopening the tab. Which API fits best?","o":["localStorage","sessionStorage","A global variable","document.title"],"a":[0],"e":"localStorage persists across sessions until it is cleared. sessionStorage is cleared when the tab closes, and global variables disappear when the page unloads."},{"id":"jsd-1sun4qr","d":"browser","m":false,"q":"What does the Network panel in browser developer tools help a developer investigate?","o":["The requests a page makes, with their timing, status codes and payloads","The memory addresses of JavaScript variables","The Git history of the project","The order in which CSS rules are written in the source file"],"a":[0],"e":"The Network panel lists each request and response, which is how a developer confirms an API call fired, how long it took and what it returned."},{"id":"jsd-1mx8n7","d":"browser","m":false,"q":"Which API should a developer use to ask the browser for the user's current location, knowing that the user may refuse?","o":["navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition with a success and an error callback","window.location.get()","document.geolocation","navigator.gps()"],"a":[0],"e":"The Geolocation API is exposed on navigator.geolocation. Access requires user permission, so the code must handle the error callback for a denied request."},{"id":"jsd-1whcvcq","d":"debug","m":false,"q":"What does this code log?\n```js\ntry {\n  JSON.parse('{ bad json }');\n} catch (e) {\n  console.log(e.name);\n} finally {\n  console.log('done');\n}\n```","o":["SyntaxError then done","done only","SyntaxError only","TypeError then done"],"a":[0],"e":"Invalid JSON text makes JSON.parse throw a SyntaxError, the catch block logs its name, and the finally block always runs afterwards."},{"id":"jsd-hy61mz","d":"debug","m":false,"q":"A developer wants to pause code at a specific line, inspect variables and step through execution in the browser. What should they use?","o":["A breakpoint in the Sources panel, or a debugger statement","console.table","A try and catch block","window.alert"],"a":[0],"e":"Breakpoints stop execution so the call stack and scope variables can be inspected and stepped through. console methods only print values, and alert interrupts the page without inspection tools."},{"id":"jsd-1l1os4k","d":"debug","m":false,"q":"Which statement about throwing errors is correct?","o":["Throwing an Error object preserves a stack trace and a message.","Only strings can be thrown.","A thrown error is always caught by the browser silently.","throw returns a value to the caller like return does."],"a":[0],"e":"Any value can be thrown, but throwing Error objects is the recommended practice because they carry a stack. An uncaught exception unwinds the call stack until a catch block handles it."},{"id":"jsd-e3bkwd","d":"debug","m":false,"q":"Which console method is the best choice for showing an array of objects as a sortable table?","o":["console.table","console.warn","console.assert","console.clear"],"a":[0],"e":"console.table renders arrays and objects as a table with columns for each property, which makes comparing records easy."},{"id":"jsd-1omm4s3","d":"async","m":false,"q":"What is the order of the output?\n```js\nconsole.log('A');\nsetTimeout(() => console.log('B'), 0);\nPromise.resolve().then(() => console.log('C'));\nconsole.log('D');\n```","o":["A D C B","A B C D","A C D B","A D B C"],"a":[0],"e":"Synchronous code runs first, giving A and D. Promise callbacks go on the microtask queue, which is drained before the next task, so C runs before the timeout callback B, even though its delay is zero."},{"id":"jsd-1rhdrdb","d":"async","m":false,"q":"What does this code log?\n```js\nasync function load() {\n  return 42;\n}\nconst result = load();\nconsole.log(result instanceof Promise);\n```","o":["true","false","42","undefined"],"a":[0],"e":"An async function always returns a promise. The returned value 42 becomes the resolved value of that promise, and the caller must use await or then to get it."},{"id":"jsd-1c995gu","d":"async","m":false,"q":"A developer needs to start three independent API calls at the same time and continue only after all of them succeed. Which approach should they use?","o":["await Promise.all([callA(), callB(), callC()])","await callA(); await callB(); await callC();","Promise.race([callA(), callB(), callC()])","setTimeout on each call"],"a":[0],"e":"Promise.all runs the promises concurrently and resolves with all results, or rejects as soon as one fails. Awaiting one call after another runs them sequentially, and race settles with whichever finishes first."},{"id":"jsd-slyqn","d":"async","m":false,"q":"What does this code log?\n```js\nasync function run() {\n  try {\n    await Promise.reject(new Error('fail'));\n    console.log('after');\n  } catch (e) {\n    console.log(e.message);\n  }\n}\nrun();\n```","o":["fail","after","fail then after","Nothing, the rejection is unhandled"],"a":[0],"e":"Awaiting a rejected promise throws the rejection reason inside the async function, so the catch block handles it and the line after the await never runs."},{"id":"jsd-8060nd","d":"async","m":false,"q":"Which statement about the JavaScript event loop is correct?","o":["The call stack must be empty before queued callbacks are run.","JavaScript runs several functions at the same time on separate threads.","A callback can interrupt a function that is currently running.","Promises are processed after all timers."],"a":[0],"e":"JavaScript runs one piece of code at a time. Queued tasks and microtasks wait until the current call stack is empty, and microtasks such as promise callbacks are processed before the next timer task."},{"id":"jsd-1zb2sb","d":"async","m":false,"q":"A developer wants a function to pause between retries without blocking the page. Which code does that?","o":["await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 1000));","while (Date.now() < end) {}","setTimeout(1000);","sleep(1000);"],"a":[0],"e":"Wrapping setTimeout in a promise lets an async function wait without blocking the event loop. A busy loop freezes the page, and there is no built-in sleep function."},{"id":"jsd-76fquh","d":"server","m":false,"q":"Which Node.js command installs the dependencies listed in package.json?","o":["npm install","npm run","node install","npm publish"],"a":[0],"e":"npm install reads package.json and installs the listed dependencies into node_modules. npm publish uploads a package to a registry, and npm run executes a script."},{"id":"jsd-lfprz1","d":"server","m":false,"q":"What is the purpose of the devDependencies section of package.json?","o":["It lists packages needed for development and testing, not at run time.","It lists packages that are installed only in production.","It lists packages that are never installed.","It holds the scripts that start the application."],"a":[0],"e":"devDependencies hold tools such as test runners and linters. They are installed in development, and are skipped when installing with the production-only option."},{"id":"jsd-1ri565f","d":"server","m":false,"q":"Which Node.js core module is used to read a file from disk?","o":["fs","http","path","events"],"a":[0],"e":"The fs module provides file system operations. http creates servers and clients, path builds and parses file paths, and events provides the EventEmitter class."},{"id":"jsd-oulw0f","d":"server","m":false,"q":"A developer wants a Node.js program to start a basic web server that responds to requests. Which core module should they use?","o":["http","os","fs","util"],"a":[0],"e":"The http module provides createServer to accept requests and send responses. fs, os and util do not listen on network ports."},{"id":"jsd-ivi9lk","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"Consider this function and its test.\n```js\nfunction isAdult(age) { return age > 18; }\ntest('18 is adult', () => { expect(isAdult(20)).toBe(true); });\n```\nThe requirement says a person aged 18 or over is an adult. What is wrong with the test?","o":["It misses the boundary value 18, so the bug in the comparison goes unnoticed.","It should use toEqual instead of toBe.","Tests must not call the function directly.","Nothing, the test fully covers the requirement."],"a":[0],"e":"The function uses > instead of >=, so 18 is wrongly rejected. A test that only uses 20 passes anyway. Boundary values such as exactly 18 expose off-by-one errors."},{"id":"jsd-1ua76e0","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"Which practice makes a unit test more effective?","o":["Testing one behaviour per test and asserting on the specific expected result","Asserting only that the function does not throw","Sharing mutable state between tests so they run faster","Calling real production services in every test"],"a":[0],"e":"Focused tests with precise assertions fail for a clear reason. Weak assertions pass even when the logic is wrong, and shared state or live services make tests flaky."},{"id":"jsd-2a1lu1","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"A function sends data with fetch. How should a unit test avoid making a real network call?","o":["Replace fetch with a mock or stub that returns a controlled response","Run the test only when the network is available","Remove the fetch call from the production code","Increase the test timeout"],"a":[0],"e":"Mocking the dependency keeps the test fast, repeatable and independent of the network, and it lets the test simulate error responses too."},{"id":"jsd-1vpvbr3","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"A test passes when the code is correct but also still passes when the code under test is replaced by a function that always returns true. What does that show?","o":["The assertions are too weak to verify the real behaviour.","The test is a good integration test.","The test is correct because it never fails.","The code under test is too complicated."],"a":[0],"e":"A test that cannot fail for a wrong implementation proves nothing. Strengthen it with assertions on concrete values and with cases that should produce a negative result."}]},"pd2":{"id":"pd2","short":"Platform Developer II","name":"Salesforce Certified Platform Developer II","blurb":"Advanced Apex, integration patterns, async processing, UI components, testing, deployment and performance.","exam":{"questions":60,"unscored":"up to 5 unscored","minutes":120,"passing":70,"fee":"US$200 (retake US$100)","release":"Winter '24","guide":"https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=005298967&language=en_US&type=1","trailhead":"https://trailhead.salesforce.com/credentials/platformdeveloperii"},"domains":[{"n":8,"id":"fundamentals","name":"Advanced Developer Fundamentals","pct":15},{"n":14,"id":"logic","name":"Process Automation, Logic, and Integration","pct":27},{"n":10,"id":"ui","name":"User Interface","pct":20},{"n":10,"id":"testing","name":"Testing, Debugging, and Deployment","pct":20},{"n":8,"id":"performance","name":"Performance","pct":18}],"questions":[{"id":"pd2-1ybxvgc","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"An org uses multiple currencies with dated exchange rates turned on. A developer must show opportunity amounts in the running user's currency in a SOQL result. Which approach is correct?","o":["Use the convertCurrency() function in the SELECT clause","Multiply Amount by an exchange rate hard-coded in Apex","Query the CurrencyIsoCode field and divide in a formula field","Call UserInfo.getLocale() and adjust the amount"],"a":[0],"e":"convertCurrency() converts currency fields in the query result to the user's currency using the org's exchange rates. Hard-coded rates go stale, and locale describes number and date formats, not currency."},{"id":"pd2-i00gm8","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"A developer needs to give a specific user read access to one custom Project__c record, in code, because no sharing rule can express the logic. What should they create?","o":["A record in the Project__Share object with a custom Apex sharing reason as the RowCause","A new role in the role hierarchy for the record","A field-level security setting on Project__c","A permission set that grants View All on Project__c"],"a":[0],"e":"Apex managed sharing inserts rows into the object's share table with an Apex sharing reason, which survives owner changes and can only be changed by code. Roles, field security and View All are not record-by-record grants."},{"id":"pd2-yf2os7","d":"fundamentals","m":true,"q":"Which TWO statements about Apex managed sharing are true? (Choose 2)","o":["It is available only for custom objects and some standard objects that have a share table.","Rows with an Apex sharing reason are kept when the record owner changes.","It gives the Modify All Data permission to the shared user.","It works only when the object's organisation-wide default is Public Read/Write.","It is created through the Sharing Settings page in Setup."],"a":[0,1],"e":"Share rows use a custom RowCause defined in Setup for custom objects, and unlike manual shares they are preserved when ownership changes. Sharing can only add access above the organisation-wide default, so it makes sense when the default is Private or Public Read Only."},{"id":"pd2-efkomg","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"A developer needs configuration values that admins can edit, that deploy together with the metadata between orgs, and that Apex can read with getInstance() without running a query. What should they use?","o":["Custom metadata types","Custom objects","Hierarchy custom settings","Static resources"],"a":[0],"e":"Custom metadata type records are metadata, so they travel in change sets, packages and source deployments, and Apex can read them with getInstance() or getAll() without a SOQL query. Custom setting data, by contrast, is not deployed with the metadata, and custom objects need a query."},{"id":"pd2-1j1jd8j","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"A company wants a numeric threshold that varies by user and profile and falls back to an org default. Which feature is designed for this?","o":["A hierarchy custom setting","A list custom setting","A custom metadata type","A custom label"],"a":[0],"e":"Hierarchy custom settings resolve the value by checking the user, then the profile, then the organisation default. A list setting has no hierarchy, and custom labels are translatable text."},{"id":"pd2-1grhvm4","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"What is the correct way to check in Apex whether the current user has a custom permission named Can_Approve?","o":["FeatureManagement.checkPermission('Can_Approve')","UserInfo.hasPermission('Can_Approve')","Schema.getGlobalDescribe().get('Can_Approve')","System.runAs('Can_Approve')"],"a":[0],"e":"FeatureManagement.checkPermission returns true when the running user has the custom permission through a profile or permission set."},{"id":"pd2-kcmrcr","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"A class must handle both a Contact and a Lead without knowing the type at compile time and set the Description field if it exists. Which approach is appropriate?","o":["Use the generic SObject type with sObject.getSObjectType().getDescribe().fields.getMap() and put()","Use Type.forName('Contact').newInstance() and a cast","Use a trigger on both objects","Use two separate classes with copy-pasted logic only"],"a":[0],"e":"The SObject type supports dynamic field access with put and get, and the describe information tells the code whether the field exists. This avoids duplicate code for each object."},{"id":"pd2-q4rxw3","d":"fundamentals","m":false,"q":"A developer builds an AppExchange package that must display a price in the buyer's language and number format. Which API provides the locale for the running user?","o":["UserInfo.getLocale()","UserInfo.getTimeZone()","System.today()","Schema.SObjectType.User"],"a":[0],"e":"UserInfo.getLocale returns the user's locale, such as en_US, which determines number, date and currency formatting. The time zone method returns only the zone."},{"id":"pd2-1yzn176","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"Which trigger design is recommended as a best practice?","o":["One trigger per object that delegates to a handler class and is bulk-safe","One trigger per event, all with logic written in the trigger body","Triggers that query inside a for loop for each record","Triggers that hard-code record IDs"],"a":[0],"e":"A single trigger per object gives predictable ordering, and moving logic into a handler class keeps the trigger thin, testable and easy to control. Bulk safety avoids governor limit failures when many records arrive together."},{"id":"pd2-bkkde9","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"What is the issue with this trigger code?\n```apex\ntrigger OppTrigger on Opportunity (after update) {\n    for (Opportunity o : Trigger.new) {\n        Account a = [SELECT Id, Rating FROM Account WHERE Id = :o.AccountId];\n        a.Rating = 'Hot';\n        update a;\n    }\n}\n```","o":["It runs a query and a DML statement inside a loop and will hit governor limits on bulk loads.","It must be a before trigger to update an Account.","Trigger.new cannot be used in an after update trigger.","It lacks the with sharing keyword."],"a":[0],"e":"With 200 records the loop issues 200 queries and 200 DML statements, which exceeds the limit of 100 queries in a synchronous transaction. Collect the account IDs, query once into a map, and update a list once."},{"id":"pd2-14gsgwn","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A developer needs a trigger on Account that updates Contacts and must stop the trigger from running its logic again when its own update fires the trigger a second time. What is the best approach?","o":["Track processed record IDs in a static Set so each record is handled once per transaction","Delete the trigger and use a scheduled job","Use a static Boolean that is set to true and never reset","Catch the recursion error and ignore it"],"a":[0],"e":"A static set of IDs lets later records still be processed while avoiding repeat work on those already handled. A single static Boolean can skip records that legitimately need processing in a later batch of the same transaction."},{"id":"pd2-1hvdusi","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A developer wants to insert a list of records, let the valid ones succeed and capture errors for the invalid ones. Which call should they use?","o":["Database.insert(records, false) and inspect the SaveResult list","insert records inside a try and catch only","Database.insert(records, true)","Database.upsert with a rollback"],"a":[0],"e":"Passing false for allOrNone allows partial success, and each SaveResult tells whether a record succeeded and what errors occurred. The default behaviour of a plain insert statement is all or nothing."},{"id":"pd2-1nbou3f","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"Which code correctly rolls back database changes made before an error in the same transaction?","o":["Set a Savepoint with Database.setSavepoint() and call Database.rollback(sp)","Call System.abortJob()","Call Database.rollback() with no argument","Use the final keyword on the insert"],"a":[0],"e":"A savepoint marks a point in the transaction, and Database.rollback(sp) undoes DML since that point. Rollback needs the savepoint object."},{"id":"pd2-drnm2l","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A trigger must start a callout to an external system after a Case is inserted. The callout cannot run directly in the trigger. What is the correct solution?","o":["Enqueue a Queueable class that implements Database.AllowsCallouts","Make the trigger a before insert trigger and call Http.send","Use a static variable to hold the response","Wrap the callout in a try and catch block"],"a":[0],"e":"Synchronous callouts from triggers are not allowed, and callouts after uncommitted DML in the same context fail. A Queueable or future method with callouts allowed runs later in its own transaction."},{"id":"pd2-dp72e2","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A developer sees the error You have uncommitted work pending. Please commit or rollback before calling out. How can they fix the problem?","o":["Perform the callout before the DML, or move one of them to an asynchronous job","Add a try and catch around the DML","Increase the callout timeout","Call Database.commit()"],"a":[0],"e":"Salesforce does not allow a callout after DML in the same transaction because the database could not roll back an external call. Reordering or separating the work into two transactions solves it."},{"id":"pd2-weuyt8","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"Which statement about Queueable Apex is correct?","o":["It can accept complex types such as sObjects as member variables and can chain another job.","It can only accept primitive arguments, like @future methods.","It can be scheduled only from the user interface.","It always runs synchronously in the current transaction."],"a":[0],"e":"Unlike future methods, Queueable classes can hold sObjects and custom types, return a job ID and enqueue another Queueable job from execute."},{"id":"pd2-xtrdoq","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A nightly process must handle five million Account records and update a field on each. Which solution is the best fit?","o":["Batch Apex using Database.QueryLocator in the start method","A future method that receives a list of IDs","A trigger on Account","A Queueable class that loops through all records in one transaction"],"a":[0],"e":"Batch Apex splits the work into chunks, each with fresh governor limits, and a QueryLocator can return up to 50 million records. A single transaction would exceed limits."},{"id":"pd2-yg4n59","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"What is the best way to prevent SOQL injection in a dynamic query that filters by user-entered text?","o":["Use a bind variable in Database.queryWithBinds or in a Database.query string","Concatenate the text and call replace on the double quote character","Run the query in without sharing mode","Convert the text to upper case"],"a":[0],"e":"Bind variables are treated as values and never as query syntax. If concatenation is unavoidable, String.escapeSingleQuotes is a fallback, but binds are the stronger choice."},{"id":"pd2-kgk1p0","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"A developer publishes a platform event in a trigger and wants subscribers to receive the event only if the publishing transaction commits. What should they configure?","o":["Set the event's publish behavior to Publish After Commit","Set the event's publish behavior to Publish Immediately","Subscribe with a flow only","Use a future method to publish the event"],"a":[0],"e":"With Publish After Commit, the event is published only when the transaction succeeds, so a rollback discards it. Publish Immediately sends it right away even if the transaction later fails."},{"id":"pd2-19djusy","d":"logic","m":true,"q":"Which TWO statements about an Apex trigger that subscribes to a platform event are true? (Choose 2)","o":["It runs in its own transaction, separate from the publisher.","A subscriber can resume from a stored replay ID after an outage.","It runs as the user who published the event.","It receives events only from the same transaction.","It cannot use DML."],"a":[0,1],"e":"Platform event triggers run asynchronously in their own transaction as the Automated Process user by default, and replay IDs let a subscriber catch up on events retained during the retention window."},{"id":"pd2-4eehts","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"An external system needs to create a Salesforce Lead through a custom endpoint with a JSON body. Which Apex feature should the developer use?","o":["A global class with @RestResource and an @HttpPost method","A class with @AuraEnabled methods","A scheduled Apex class","A Visualforce page with a standard controller"],"a":[0],"e":"@RestResource exposes an Apex class as a REST endpoint, and the HTTP annotations map methods to verbs. AuraEnabled methods are for Lightning components."},{"id":"pd2-n5hm6f","d":"logic","m":false,"q":"Where should credentials and the base URL of an external service be stored so they do not appear in Apex code?","o":["In a named credential","In a static final String in the class","In a custom label","In a debug log filter"],"a":[0],"e":"Named credentials hold the endpoint and authentication in one place, and the callout uses the callout: prefix, so secrets are not in code and can differ per environment."},{"id":"pd2-1kxxhi0","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A Lightning web component needs to call an Apex method that only reads data, and the component should reuse a client-side cache. Which annotation setup is required?","o":["@AuraEnabled(cacheable=true) on the method","@RemoteAction on the method","@InvocableMethod on the method","@future on the method"],"a":[0],"e":"Cacheable methods can be called with @wire and benefit from the client-side cache, but they must not perform DML."},{"id":"pd2-1gk8l3m","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A component displays data from a cacheable Apex method through @wire. After the user saves a related record, the data is stale. What should the developer call?","o":["refreshApex with the wired result","location.reload()","clearInterval","Database.refresh()"],"a":[0],"e":"refreshApex tells the wire service to re-run the provisioned query and update the component, so the page does not need a reload."},{"id":"pd2-1i358co","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A child Lightning web component must tell its parent that an item was selected. How should it do this?","o":["Dispatch a CustomEvent from the child and handle it in the parent template","Call a method on the parent through this.parent","Write to a global variable that the parent polls","Update a property on the parent object directly"],"a":[0],"e":"Data flows down through public properties and up through events. The child dispatches a CustomEvent and the parent listens with an on handler in its markup."},{"id":"pd2-tk5rwc","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"Two Lightning web components that are not in the same parent and child chain must exchange messages. Which solution is most suitable?","o":["Lightning Message Service with a message channel","Pub-sub using window globals","A shared Apex static variable","Visualforce page parameters"],"a":[0],"e":"Lightning Message Service lets components on a page, even across different frameworks like Aura, LWC and Visualforce, communicate through a message channel."},{"id":"pd2-11vldm","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"When should a developer choose Aura over Lightning Web Components?","o":["When they need a feature that LWC does not yet support, such as certain Aura-only events or components","Whenever performance matters","For all new development","When they want standard web components"],"a":[0],"e":"Lightning Web Components are the recommended model for new development, but Aura is still used where an Aura-only capability is required or in existing components."},{"id":"pd2-bmob7p","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A Visualforce page must refresh only a small area of the page after a button click without reloading the whole page. What should the developer use?","o":["The reRender attribute on an apex:commandButton with an apex:outputPanel target","apex:include","A redirect with PageReference","An iframe with a new page"],"a":[0],"e":"reRender runs the action through the controller and replaces only the listed components in the page using AJAX."},{"id":"pd2-137u11c","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"In an LWC, a developer needs to load a third-party JavaScript library stored as a static resource. Which method is correct?","o":["Import the resource with @salesforce/resourceUrl and call loadScript from lightning/platformResourceLoader","Add a script tag to the component HTML","Use document.write in connectedCallback","Reference the file with a relative path"],"a":[0],"e":"LWC does not allow arbitrary script tags. platformResourceLoader loads the static resource and returns a promise when it is ready."},{"id":"pd2-gh2raf","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A developer wants to show a success message to the user after a record is saved in an LWC. Which approach is standard?","o":["Dispatch a ShowToastEvent from lightning/platformShowToastEvent","Call alert()","Use console.log","Write text into the DOM with innerHTML"],"a":[0],"e":"ShowToastEvent displays a platform toast with title, message and variant, which matches the Salesforce experience."},{"id":"pd2-1pz31iu","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A developer wants a component layout to rearrange from three columns on desktop to one column on a phone. Which feature should they use?","o":["lightning-layout with lightning-layout-item and the size, mediumDeviceSize and smallDeviceSize attributes","Fixed pixel widths in inline styles","Separate components for each device with a user agent check","A table with a fixed width"],"a":[0],"e":"The responsive size attributes let a layout item change its column span by device breakpoint without custom code."},{"id":"pd2-1cjl69d","d":"ui","m":false,"q":"A custom form built with lightning-record-edit-form must show a field-level validation message that came from the server. Which component shows the errors?","o":["lightning-messages","lightning-card","lightning-output-field","lightning-badge"],"a":[0],"e":"lightning-messages, placed inside the record edit form, shows server-side and validation errors returned when the form is submitted."},{"id":"pd2-13o9eic","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"Why should the code that triggers an asynchronous job be placed between Test.startTest() and Test.stopTest()?","o":["stopTest forces the asynchronous work to run synchronously before the next line","startTest raises the code coverage percentage","It makes the job run in a different org","It disables governor limits for the test"],"a":[0],"e":"Test.stopTest executes queued future, queueable and batch jobs started after startTest so the test can assert on their results. The block also gets a fresh set of governor limits."},{"id":"pd2-15oz8wq","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"A test needs the same set of accounts for all its test methods and wants to avoid re-creating them each time. What should the developer use?","o":["A method annotated with @testSetup","Static variables initialised by the first test","@isTest(SeeAllData=true)","A custom setting"],"a":[0],"e":"A @testSetup method runs once, and the data it creates is available in each test method with changes rolled back between methods."},{"id":"pd2-1ogz92h","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"A developer must test a callout without calling the real service. What are the correct steps?","o":["Implement HttpCalloutMock and register it with Test.setMock(HttpCalloutMock.class, mockInstance)","Remove the callout during tests with an if statement on Test.isRunningTest","Add the remote site setting for the test endpoint","Use System.runAs"],"a":[0],"e":"Test.setMock tells the runtime to return the mock response instead of calling out, since real callouts are not allowed in tests."},{"id":"pd2-1f7h7oi","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"A developer wants to test code that depends on another class without setting up all that class's behaviour. Which Apex feature allows a stub object to be created at run time?","o":["The Stub API with System.StubProvider and Test.createStub","Test.setMock","@testVisible","Database.setSavepoint"],"a":[0],"e":"Test.createStub builds a stub for a class using a StubProvider implementation that decides what each method returns, so unit tests can isolate dependencies."},{"id":"pd2-uvth6c","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"A test must verify that a user with a limited profile cannot edit a record. How should the test run the code as that user?","o":["Create the user and wrap the code in System.runAs(user)","Call UserInfo.setUser","Log in with a different browser","Set SeeAllData to true"],"a":[0],"e":"runAs executes a block under the given user's sharing, record access and permissions, though it does not enforce all license limitations."},{"id":"pd2-14imogn","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"A developer sees an exception in a trigger only in production. Which tool lets them reproduce the execution later by loading the log with stepping and variable inspection?","o":["The Apex Replay Debugger in Salesforce Extensions for VS Code","The Developer Console Query Editor","A change set comparison","The Data Import Wizard"],"a":[0],"e":"Replay Debugger reads a debug log and lets the developer step through the code and inspect variables without having to re-run the transaction."},{"id":"pd2-1vi1t2","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"A team wants source-driven development with disposable environments. Which combination is most appropriate?","o":["Scratch orgs created from a project definition file and source tracking with version control","A single shared sandbox edited by all developers","Change sets built by hand","Direct changes in production"],"a":[0],"e":"Scratch orgs are created from configuration in source control, are short-lived and track source changes, so teams can develop and test in isolation and deploy from the repository."},{"id":"pd2-121qdes","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"An unlocked package is chosen over a change set for deployment. What is one benefit?","o":["The package is versioned and its contents can be installed or upgraded repeatably in other orgs.","It removes the need for tests.","It works only in production orgs.","It deploys data records as well as metadata."],"a":[0],"e":"Unlocked packages bundle metadata into versions that can be installed and upgraded, which supports a repeatable pipeline. They still require tests to meet deployment rules."},{"id":"pd2-141te9e","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"A test publishes a platform event and then needs the subscriber trigger to process it before the assertions. Which method helps?","o":["Test.getEventBus().deliver()","Test.stopTest() only","System.debug on the event","Database.insert on the event"],"a":[0],"e":"Platform event delivery in tests can be controlled by calling deliver on the test event bus, or by calling stopTest, which also delivers events. deliver makes the timing explicit."},{"id":"pd2-140dxt4","d":"testing","m":false,"q":"A deployment to production fails because the org-wide code coverage is below the required threshold. What does the minimum require?","o":["At least 75 percent of Apex lines covered by tests, and all tests passing","100 percent coverage for each class","Coverage only for triggers","Coverage only for classes that have been changed"],"a":[0],"e":"Salesforce requires at least 75 percent overall coverage for deployments to production, and each trigger must have some coverage. Meeting the number does not replace meaningful assertions."},{"id":"pd2-oc12r5","d":"performance","m":false,"q":"A query on a large object is slow. The WHERE clause filters on a custom text field that is not indexed. What is the best fix?","o":["Ask Salesforce Support to create a custom index on the field, or mark it as an external ID, and filter selectively","Add ORDER BY to the query","Wrap the query in a try and catch block","Query the object twice"],"a":[0],"e":"Selective queries use an index, and a non-indexed filter on a big object leads to a full scan. External IDs and unique fields are indexed automatically, and Support can add a custom index to other fields."},{"id":"pd2-z79kex","d":"performance","m":false,"q":"Which filter is most likely to make a SOQL query non-selective?","o":["A negative operator such as != or NOT IN on an indexed field","An equality filter on the record Id","An equality filter on an external ID field","A filter on a lookup field that is indexed"],"a":[0],"e":"Negative operators, leading wildcards in LIKE, and filters on fields with a low number of distinct values usually cannot use an index efficiently. Id and external ID filters are the most selective."},{"id":"pd2-kv9515","d":"performance","m":false,"q":"A developer wants to find out how Salesforce will run a SOQL query and which indexes it will use. Which tool should they use?","o":["The Query Plan tool in the Developer Console","The Execute Anonymous window","The Apex Test Execution page","The Event Monitoring log"],"a":[0],"e":"The Query Plan tool shows the cost of each possible plan and which index would be used, so a developer can tune a query before it fails in production."},{"id":"pd2-1asfn8f","d":"performance","m":false,"q":"Which technique reduces heap usage when an Apex method processes a very large number of records returned by a query?","o":["Use a SOQL for loop that processes records in batches of 200","Assign all records to a List and process afterwards","Use a static variable to store all results","Use a future method for every record"],"a":[0],"e":"A SOQL for loop retrieves records in chunks as they are needed, which keeps heap small. Loading all records into a list consumes heap quickly."},{"id":"pd2-wsjgs8","d":"performance","m":false,"q":"A Visualforce page with a large list view state is slow and hits the view state limit. What should the developer do?","o":["Mark variables that are not needed between requests as transient","Increase the page timeout","Convert all variables to static","Add more rerender tags"],"a":[0],"e":"Transient variables are not saved in the view state, so the page transmits less data. Fewer retained collections also reduces the round trip cost."},{"id":"pd2-538oqi","d":"performance","m":false,"q":"A page renders data from a large table. Which choice improves perceived performance for users?","o":["Load the first set of records and use pagination or lazy loading for the rest","Load every record when the page opens","Disable the browser cache","Run a synchronous callout for each row"],"a":[0],"e":"Showing a limited page of data reduces query time, payload size and rendering work. Users still reach the rest through paging or scroll loading."},{"id":"pd2-n99blc","d":"performance","m":false,"q":"Which approach lets an Apex class avoid querying the same rarely changing reference data for every request?","o":["Store it in Platform Cache","Store it in a custom field on User","Store it in a debug log","Call the data with an @future method each time"],"a":[0],"e":"Platform Cache keeps data in memory for faster access across requests, reducing repeated queries. The developer must still handle cache misses and refresh."},{"id":"pd2-6zb8k7","d":"performance","m":false,"q":"A synchronous Apex transaction is nearing the CPU time limit because of nested loops over large lists. What is the most effective improvement?","o":["Replace repeated list searches with a Map keyed by the field being matched","Increase the test coverage","Move the loops to a Visualforce controller","Add more debug statements"],"a":[0],"e":"Map lookups take constant time, while searching through a list for every element grows with the square of the data size. Removing nested loops cuts CPU time directly."}]},"sales":{"id":"sales","short":"Agentforce Sales Consultant","name":"Salesforce Certified Agentforce Sales Consultant (formerly Sales Cloud Consultant)","blurb":"Sales lifecycle, consulting and implementation, sales process design, data management and sales AI.","exam":{"questions":60,"unscored":"up to 5 unscored","minutes":105,"passing":73,"fee":"US$200 (retake US$100)","release":"Summer '25","guide":"https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=005298976&language=en_US&type=1","trailhead":"https://trailhead.salesforce.com/credentials/salescloudconsultant"},"domains":[{"n":10,"id":"lifecycle","name":"Sales Lifecycle","pct":20},{"n":12,"id":"consulting","name":"Consulting and Implementation Strategies","pct":25},{"n":12,"id":"practical","name":"Practical Application of Agentforce Sales Expertise","pct":24},{"n":9,"id":"data","name":"Data Management","pct":18},{"n":7,"id":"ai","name":"Predictive and Generative AI","pct":13}],"questions":[{"id":"sal-1b4t3d6","d":"lifecycle","m":false,"q":"A sales director wants to see, for each rep, how much pipeline is in each opportunity stage. Which report format is the best starting point?","o":["A summary report on Opportunities grouped by owner, with a second grouping by stage","A tabular report with no groupings","A joined report of Leads and Accounts","A dashboard component with no source report"],"a":[0],"e":"Summary reports let users group rows and show subtotals, so a grouping by owner and then stage gives the pipeline by rep and stage. Tabular reports cannot group, and dashboards need a source report."},{"id":"sal-114vesa","d":"lifecycle","m":false,"q":"A company wants to forecast revenue by the rep's own expected quota attainment and let managers adjust the numbers of their team. Which feature supports this?","o":["Collaborative Forecasts with forecast hierarchy based on the role hierarchy","A custom object for forecasts with workflow","The Opportunity Pipeline report only","A formula field on the Account"],"a":[0],"e":"Collaborative Forecasts roll up opportunity data through a forecast hierarchy, and managers can adjust their team's amounts. The pipeline report shows data but offers no adjustment or rollup by quota."},{"id":"sal-sf3b30","d":"lifecycle","m":false,"q":"Sales reps are overloaded with manual follow-ups. Which feature lets reps work a prioritised list of leads and contacts with a guided sequence of calls and emails?","o":["Sales Engagement with cadences and the Work Queue","Web-to-Lead","Chatter groups","Campaign member statuses"],"a":[0],"e":"Sales Engagement lets managers define a cadence of steps, and reps work through their prioritised tasks from the Work Queue. Web-to-Lead captures leads and does not guide follow-up."},{"id":"sal-ju9em8","d":"lifecycle","m":true,"q":"Which TWO benefits does Opportunity Teams provide? (Choose 2)","o":["Several users can share credit and access on one opportunity.","Team members can be given a role and a specific access level on that opportunity.","It automatically creates a new opportunity for every team member.","It replaces the need for a role hierarchy.","It changes the organisation-wide default for Accounts."],"a":[0,1],"e":"Opportunity Teams add people to a single record with team roles, and access can be granted at read or edit level. Teams do not duplicate records or replace the hierarchy."},{"id":"sal-xus6jp","d":"lifecycle","m":false,"q":"A customer asks which feature is used to model different sales processes, for example one for new business and one for renewals, each with its own stages. What should the consultant recommend?","o":["Record types with separate sales processes","Multiple opportunity objects","Separate page layouts only","Validation rules"],"a":[0],"e":"A sales process lists the stage values available for opportunities, and a record type is linked to one process, so each type of deal can have its own stages."},{"id":"sal-chsdsx","d":"lifecycle","m":false,"q":"A team wants leads from the website to be assigned to reps by region automatically, with a fallback owner for unmatched leads. What should the admin configure?","o":["Lead assignment rules, with a final rule entry that has no criteria","A validation rule on Lead owner","A sharing rule on the Lead object","A workflow on the User object"],"a":[0],"e":"Assignment rules evaluate entries in order, and a last entry without criteria catches anything that does not match, assigning it to a default owner. Sharing rules give access but do not set ownership."},{"id":"sal-crtqv9","d":"lifecycle","m":false,"q":"A sales manager asks how to track how many days opportunities stay in each stage. What should the consultant suggest?","o":["Opportunity History or the stage duration data in standard reports","A trigger that counts days","A new Chatter feed","A custom object per stage"],"a":[0],"e":"Opportunity field history tracks stage changes, and reports on history can show how long deals spent in each stage. No custom code is needed."},{"id":"sal-1jdq5ky","d":"lifecycle","m":false,"q":"Which feature gives sales reps a view of recommended next actions and key deals to focus on, on the home page, built from their data?","o":["Sales Cloud Home with Pipeline Inspection and key deals highlights","The Setup audit trail","The Data Import Wizard","The Developer Console"],"a":[0],"e":"Sales Cloud Home and Pipeline Inspection give reps and managers a single view of deal changes and priorities. The other options are administration tools, not sales workspaces."},{"id":"sal-17lo8pz","d":"lifecycle","m":false,"q":"A company sells through partners and wants partners to register deals and see only their own opportunities. Which solution matches best?","o":["An Experience Cloud partner site with partner roles and sharing","Chatter free licences","A public Web-to-Lead form","Email-to-Case"],"a":[0],"e":"Partner Relationship Management on Experience Cloud gives external users controlled access to leads, opportunities and deal registration through partner roles and sharing."},{"id":"sal-1phe84x","d":"lifecycle","m":true,"q":"A user cannot find an opportunity they believe they should see. The org-wide default for Opportunity is Private. Which TWO items could grant them access? (Choose 2)","o":["They are in a role above the owner in the hierarchy.","They were added to the opportunity team.","They have the Chatter Free licence.","They are in a different time zone.","They have a different currency set."],"a":[0,1],"e":"With a private default, access comes from ownership, the role hierarchy, sharing rules, teams and manual sharing. Licence type for Chatter, time zone and currency do not affect record access."},{"id":"sal-shyddx","d":"consulting","m":false,"q":"Before the build starts, a consultant must understand what the business needs. Which activity belongs to discovery?","o":["Running workshops with stakeholders to capture requirements and prioritise use cases","Configuring page layouts","Loading data into production","Writing Apex tests"],"a":[0],"e":"Discovery is about understanding goals, processes and pain points. Building and loading data follow once the requirements are agreed."},{"id":"sal-do76z8","d":"consulting","m":false,"q":"A project's scope keeps growing and the delivery date is at risk. What is the best way for the consultant to respond?","o":["Use a change control process to evaluate each change for impact on scope, cost and timeline","Accept every request to keep the customer happy","Stop all communication until the project ends","Rebuild the plan without telling the sponsor"],"a":[0],"e":"Change control makes the impact of each request visible, so the sponsor can decide whether to add scope, move a date or defer the item."},{"id":"sal-1qy1a39","d":"consulting","m":false,"q":"Adoption of a new sales process is low three months after go-live. What should the consultant do first?","o":["Gather feedback and usage data, such as login and field completion reports, to find the cause","Add many more required fields","Remove the training materials","Change the licences for everyone"],"a":[0],"e":"Adoption problems have many causes, including training, usability and missing value for users. Measuring first points to the right fix."},{"id":"sal-1rt5ao3","d":"consulting","m":false,"q":"Which approach to deployment lowers the risk of a large release to many sales users?","o":["A phased rollout starting with a pilot group, plus training and a feedback loop","A big-bang release without testing","Release on a Friday evening with no support plan","Deploy only to the executive team permanently"],"a":[0],"e":"A pilot lets the team find issues and refine training before the wider release, which reduces disruption."},{"id":"sal-1qub6gd","d":"consulting","m":false,"q":"A consultant is asked how to define success for a new Salesforce implementation. What should they recommend?","o":["Agree measurable success metrics, such as win rate, sales cycle length and user adoption, before the project starts","Judge success by the number of fields created","Wait until after go-live to decide on metrics","Use the number of logins only"],"a":[0],"e":"Success measures tied to business outcomes give the project a target and allow the team to show value after launch."},{"id":"sal-1dirnm9","d":"consulting","m":true,"q":"Which TWO activities are part of change management for a Salesforce rollout? (Choose 2)","o":["Communicating the benefits and timeline to users in advance","Training users and identifying champions in each team","Turning off all validation rules","Hiding the old system without notice","Limiting feedback to the project team"],"a":[0,1],"e":"Change management prepares people for the new process through communication, training and champions. Removing safeguards or skipping communication increases resistance."},{"id":"sal-1mo6u7m","d":"consulting","m":false,"q":"A client wants to use a sandbox type that holds a copy of all production data and metadata to run realistic user acceptance tests. Which should the consultant propose?","o":["A Full sandbox","A Developer sandbox","A Developer Pro sandbox","A scratch org"],"a":[0],"e":"A Full sandbox copies production metadata and data, which makes it suited for performance and acceptance testing. Developer and Developer Pro sandboxes copy metadata only, with limited data storage."},{"id":"sal-1z0e7ek","d":"consulting","m":false,"q":"During discovery, stakeholders in sales and service give conflicting requirements. What should the consultant do?","o":["Facilitate a session to understand the underlying goals and agree priorities with the sponsor","Pick the requirement of the loudest stakeholder","Implement both and let users decide later","Remove both requirements"],"a":[0],"e":"Understanding the underlying business goal and agreeing priorities with the decision-maker resolves conflicts in a way the organisation can support."},{"id":"sal-smfzdx","d":"consulting","m":false,"q":"A project is running late, and the sponsor asks to cut testing to make the date. How should the consultant advise?","o":["Explain the risks, and offer options such as reducing the scope or phasing features, while keeping the critical testing","Skip testing entirely","Move testing to after go-live without telling users","Let developers decide alone"],"a":[0],"e":"Testing protects the business from defects. Trading scope or phasing the release addresses the date without losing quality control."},{"id":"sal-mo4qxa","d":"consulting","m":false,"q":"Which technique helps a team prioritise a long list of requirements by business value and effort?","o":["A prioritisation approach such as MoSCoW or a value versus effort matrix","Alphabetical order","The order in which the requests arrived by email","The preference of the developer"],"a":[0],"e":"Structured prioritisation makes trade-offs explicit and helps stakeholders agree what goes in the first release."},{"id":"sal-1digujn","d":"consulting","m":false,"q":"A company wants a plan to keep improving Salesforce after launch. What should the consultant recommend?","o":["A governance model with a backlog, regular releases and a body that approves changes","No further changes after go-live","Allow every user to edit metadata in production","Give all changes to one developer"],"a":[0],"e":"Continuous improvement needs a way to collect, prioritise and release changes safely, which a governance structure and backlog provide."},{"id":"sal-1u461lu","d":"consulting","m":false,"q":"The project manager wants to know how to measure whether the project is on track for time and scope. Which artifact is best?","o":["A project plan with milestones and a regularly reviewed status report","A list of Chatter posts","An org chart","A report of all closed won opportunities"],"a":[0],"e":"Milestones and status reporting show progress against the plan and surface risks early."},{"id":"sal-s87vnn","d":"practical","m":false,"q":"A company needs a process that takes a lead through qualification, conversion to an account, contact and opportunity, then a quote and a closed deal. Which sequence of features supports this end to end?","o":["Leads, lead conversion, opportunities, products and price books, quotes","Cases, entitlements, milestones","Campaigns only","Knowledge articles and Chat"],"a":[0],"e":"The sales process in Sales Cloud runs from leads to converted accounts, contacts and opportunities, with products and price books feeding quotes at the end."},{"id":"sal-14ng65c","d":"practical","m":false,"q":"A sales user needs to add products to an opportunity at prices that depend on the customer's contract. Which feature should the consultant recommend?","o":["Multiple price books, with each opportunity linked to the correct one","One price book with all prices in the product name","A text field for price on the opportunity","A custom object for prices"],"a":[0],"e":"Each opportunity can use one price book, and multiple price books let the company hold different prices per segment or contract."},{"id":"sal-3lczrp","d":"practical","m":false,"q":"Opportunities close in several currencies, but sales leadership reports in a single corporate currency. What should be turned on?","o":["Multiple currencies, with a corporate currency and exchange rates","A formula field with the exchange rate typed in","A separate org for each country","A validation rule that blocks other currencies"],"a":[0],"e":"Multi-currency allows records in different currencies, while reports convert to the corporate or user currency using the maintained rates. Enabling it is permanent for the org."},{"id":"sal-2dbqf4","d":"practical","m":false,"q":"A company wants sales reps to see only their own accounts, but their manager should see everything their team owns. What is the simplest design?","o":["Set the Account organisation-wide default to Private and use the role hierarchy","Set the default to Public Read/Write","Create a sharing rule per rep","Give every rep Modify All Data"],"a":[0],"e":"A private default limits access to owners, and the role hierarchy grants managers access to records owned by those below them."},{"id":"sal-1sxhx8t","d":"practical","m":true,"q":"Which TWO options give access to accounts to users who are not the owner and not above the owner in the hierarchy? (Choose 2)","o":["Sharing rules based on owner or criteria","Account teams","A page layout assignment","A list view filter","A custom tab"],"a":[0,1],"e":"Sharing rules and teams open up records beyond the hierarchy. Layouts, list views and tabs only change what users see once they have access."},{"id":"sal-zfe3bq","d":"practical","m":false,"q":"A customer wants managers to approve any discount above 20 percent before the quote is sent to the customer. What should the consultant propose?","o":["An approval process, or a flow-based approval, on the quote","A required field on the account","A report subscription","A queue for quotes"],"a":[0],"e":"Approval processes route a record for approval based on entry criteria, such as discount percent, and lock or update the record based on the outcome."},{"id":"sal-fpy995","d":"practical","m":false,"q":"A rep needs to send a branded PDF with line items to the customer from an opportunity. Which feature produces this?","o":["Quotes with a quote template and PDF","A report export","A Chatter post","A campaign influence report"],"a":[0],"e":"Quotes pull opportunity products into a document, and quote templates define the layout of the PDF that can be emailed to the customer."},{"id":"sal-17iu5vk","d":"practical","m":false,"q":"A marketing team wants to see which campaigns influenced won opportunities. Which feature should be configured?","o":["Campaign Influence","Case milestones","Territory management","Assignment rules"],"a":[0],"e":"Campaign Influence links campaigns to opportunities so that the revenue they contributed to can be reported."},{"id":"sal-re265h","d":"practical","m":false,"q":"A company has reps in overlapping geographic regions and needs to align accounts to territories that can change each quarter, with forecasts by territory. What should the consultant recommend?","o":["Enterprise Territory Management","Role hierarchy only","Public groups","Record types"],"a":[0],"e":"Enterprise Territory Management lets accounts belong to multiple territories using rules, and supports territory forecasts and changes without altering the role hierarchy."},{"id":"sal-1l3q250","d":"practical","m":false,"q":"A rep wants to log emails sent from Outlook or Gmail against the related records automatically. Which solution does this?","o":["Einstein Activity Capture or the email integration, with Salesforce for Outlook or Gmail","A custom Apex email service","Web-to-Case","A scheduled report"],"a":[0],"e":"Email integrations and activity capture sync email and calendar events with Salesforce records, so reps do not have to log activity by hand."},{"id":"sal-mgyo4w","d":"practical","m":true,"q":"Which TWO capabilities are available when a business uses Slack with Sales Cloud? (Choose 2)","o":["Sharing record details and updates in a channel","Receiving alerts when an opportunity changes","Replacing the sales process","Removing the need for an opportunity record","Changing the org's licences"],"a":[0,1],"e":"The Slack integration brings records and notifications into channels, helping teams collaborate on deals. It does not replace the sales process or the record."},{"id":"sal-10s1hek","d":"practical","m":false,"q":"A client wants a button on the opportunity that guides reps through a set of steps and creates records at the end, with no code. Which tool should the consultant suggest?","o":["A screen flow launched from an action","An Apex trigger","A workflow field update","A Visualforce email template"],"a":[0],"e":"A screen flow guides users through inputs and can create or update records, and it can be placed on the page as an action."},{"id":"sal-ho2w5u","d":"data","m":false,"q":"A customer is moving from a legacy CRM and wants to load accounts, then contacts, then opportunities, keeping relationships intact. What should the consultant plan for?","o":["Load parents first and use external IDs to relate the child records","Load all objects in any order","Load child records first","Recreate the relationships by hand after loading"],"a":[0],"e":"Relationships need the parent to exist, and external IDs let the child file reference the parent without knowing the Salesforce ID. Loading in dependency order avoids errors."},{"id":"sal-ka328d","d":"data","m":false,"q":"Duplicate leads and contacts are reducing trust in the data. Which Salesforce features help prevent and find them?","o":["Matching rules and duplicate rules","Validation rules only","Page layouts","Report folders"],"a":[0],"e":"Matching rules define what counts as a match, and duplicate rules decide whether to block or alert users when a match is found."},{"id":"sal-1scsvcw","d":"data","m":false,"q":"A client has two million records to load once. Which tool is the most suitable?","o":["Data Loader or the Bulk API","The Data Import Wizard in the UI","Manual entry","A list view"],"a":[0],"e":"The Data Import Wizard has a lower record limit. Data Loader and the Bulk API handle large volumes and support insert, update, upsert and delete."},{"id":"sal-19isi2w","d":"data","m":false,"q":"What does an upsert operation do when a matching record is found by an external ID?","o":["It updates the existing record, and otherwise creates a new one","It always inserts a new record","It deletes the existing record","It fails with a duplicate error"],"a":[0],"e":"Upsert uses the key to decide whether to update or insert, which makes it useful for repeatable integration loads."},{"id":"sal-m1fsaw","d":"data","m":false,"q":"A company wants to keep older closed opportunities available for audit but reduce the storage cost and clutter. What should the consultant discuss?","o":["A data archiving strategy, with a plan for retention and external storage or Big Objects","Deleting all history immediately","Making all records private","Converting them to leads"],"a":[0],"e":"Archiving moves rarely used data out of the main objects while retaining access to it under a retention policy, which controls storage and keeps performance."},{"id":"sal-132biny","d":"data","m":false,"q":"A report shows missing values in a field that was meant to be mandatory. How can the admin ensure that future records are complete?","o":["Make the field required on the page layout or use a validation rule, and clean the existing data","Hide the field","Delete the field","Give users read-only access"],"a":[0],"e":"Required settings and validation rules prevent incomplete saves from now on, while a data clean-up fixes the history."},{"id":"sal-v7tl1t","d":"data","m":true,"q":"Which TWO practices improve the quality of sales data over time? (Choose 2)","o":["Use picklists and validation rules to standardise entries","Schedule reviews of duplicate and incomplete records with reports","Allow free text for every field","Remove all required fields","Let users create duplicate accounts to save time"],"a":[0,1],"e":"Standard values and regular quality reviews keep data consistent. Free text and no requirements lead to variation and gaps."},{"id":"sal-1754pee","d":"data","m":false,"q":"A solution will have hundreds of thousands of opportunities and needs fast reports. What should the consultant consider?","o":["Selective report filters, indexed fields and archiving data that is not needed","Reports with no filters","A single list view for all records","More custom fields on every record"],"a":[0],"e":"Large data volumes require filters that use indexes and careful design to avoid slow queries and report timeouts."},{"id":"sal-pa491i","d":"data","m":false,"q":"Before a migration to production, what should the team do with the load files?","o":["Test the load in a sandbox with a realistic sample and validate the results","Load directly into production without testing","Skip the mapping of fields","Delete the source system"],"a":[0],"e":"A rehearsal in a sandbox finds mapping problems, validation conflicts and performance issues before they affect real data."},{"id":"sal-1f8xe84","d":"ai","m":false,"q":"Which type of AI predicts the likelihood that a lead will convert based on historical data?","o":["Predictive AI such as lead scoring","Generative AI only","Rule-based assignment","A static report"],"a":[0],"e":"Predictive AI uses patterns in past data to estimate outcomes such as conversion likelihood. Generative AI creates new content such as text."},{"id":"sal-12qp1qk","d":"ai","m":false,"q":"A sales team wants an assistant to draft a follow-up email using details from the opportunity and the contact. Which kind of capability is this?","o":["Generative AI that uses grounding data from CRM records","A validation rule","A page layout","An assignment rule"],"a":[0],"e":"Generative AI creates text, and grounding it in CRM data keeps the draft relevant to the customer and opportunity."},{"id":"sal-1aewj6u","d":"ai","m":false,"q":"What is the purpose of the Einstein Trust Layer when a prompt is sent to a large language model?","o":["To protect data, for example by masking sensitive information and not retaining it at the model provider","To increase the length of the prompt","To store prompts in a public location","To train the model on the customer's data by default"],"a":[0],"e":"The Trust Layer adds safeguards such as data masking, zero data retention agreements and toxicity checks around model calls."},{"id":"sal-uuaxd5","d":"ai","m":true,"q":"Which TWO principles are part of using AI in an ethical way in sales scenarios? (Choose 2)","o":["Be transparent that content was generated by AI when appropriate","Review AI output before it is sent to a customer","Use customer data without consent","Allow AI to take every decision without review","Hide the source of the data"],"a":[0,1],"e":"Responsible AI use includes transparency, human review and respect for privacy. Using data without permission or removing oversight conflicts with trusted AI principles."},{"id":"sal-pbmrip","d":"ai","m":false,"q":"A manager wants insights on which opportunities are at risk based on changes in activity and engagement. Which capability fits?","o":["Pipeline Inspection with AI-driven deal insights","A static dashboard with no filters","A workflow rule","A custom object"],"a":[0],"e":"AI-driven insights flag deals that show unusual changes, so managers can focus on those that need attention."},{"id":"sal-2t8c5w","d":"ai","m":false,"q":"Before enabling a generative AI feature for sales reps, what should the consultant do about data?","o":["Check that the data the feature relies on is accurate, accessible and permitted to be used","Delete the CRM data","Give all users admin rights","Turn off field security"],"a":[0],"e":"AI output reflects the data it is given, so quality and access controls matter. Sensitive data needs to be handled under the company's policies."},{"id":"sal-149jy4e","d":"ai","m":false,"q":"A rep asks why a generated email contains a wrong product name. What is the best explanation and action?","o":["Generative output can be inaccurate, so the rep should review it and the team should improve the grounding data and prompt","The AI never makes errors","The email must be sent without reading","The org should delete all products"],"a":[0],"e":"Generated text can contain mistakes, so a human review is needed. Better grounding and clearer prompts reduce errors."}]},"service":{"id":"service","short":"Agentforce Service Consultant","name":"Salesforce Certified Agentforce Service Consultant (formerly Service Cloud Consultant)","blurb":"Contact centre strategy, service solution design, knowledge, channels, case management, analytics and integrations.","exam":{"questions":60,"unscored":"up to 5 unscored","minutes":105,"passing":78,"fee":"US$200 (retake US$100)","release":"Summer '25","guide":"https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=005298989&language=en_US&type=1","trailhead":"https://trailhead.salesforce.com/credentials/servicecloudconsultant"},"domains":[{"n":6,"id":"industry","name":"Industry Knowledge","pct":12},{"n":6,"id":"implementation","name":"Implementation Strategies","pct":12},{"n":8,"id":"design","name":"Agentforce Service Solution Design","pct":15},{"n":6,"id":"knowledge","name":"Knowledge Management","pct":12},{"n":7,"id":"channels","name":"Intake and Interaction Channels","pct":13},{"n":7,"id":"cases","name":"Case Management","pct":13},{"n":6,"id":"analytics","name":"Contact Center Analytics","pct":13},{"n":4,"id":"integrations","name":"Integrations","pct":10}],"questions":[{"id":"ser-1qpx72a","d":"industry","m":false,"q":"A contact centre director wants to reduce the time customers wait for a first answer. Which metric should the consultant track to measure this?","o":["First response time","Customer lifetime value","Pipeline coverage","Lead conversion rate"],"a":[0],"e":"First response time measures how long it takes for a customer to get the first reply after contacting support. The other measures belong to sales and marketing."},{"id":"ser-14q5t03","d":"industry","m":false,"q":"A company wants to measure how many customer issues are solved in the first contact without a follow-up. Which KPI is this?","o":["First contact resolution","Average handle time","Net promoter score","Abandon rate"],"a":[0],"e":"First contact resolution shows the share of issues solved on the first interaction. Handle time measures duration, and NPS measures loyalty."},{"id":"ser-1x8d1wv","d":"industry","m":false,"q":"A consultant explains that case deflection is a goal of the support strategy. What does it mean?","o":["Customers solve their issue through self-service, so fewer cases reach agents","Agents move cases to other agents","Cases are deleted after a set time","Customers are blocked from contacting support"],"a":[0],"e":"Deflection means customers find an answer through knowledge articles, communities or bots, so that a case is never created."},{"id":"ser-6b6wmm","d":"industry","m":false,"q":"A client reports that average handle time has increased after a new process was introduced. What is a reasonable first step for the consultant?","o":["Analyse the process steps and agent screens to find where time is being spent","Remove all quality checks","Hire more agents immediately","Change the customer survey"],"a":[0],"e":"Finding the cause of added time, for example extra clicks or missing information on the screen, leads to a targeted fix rather than a costly guess."},{"id":"ser-1dfyxcn","d":"industry","m":true,"q":"Which TWO items are risks the consultant should raise when a client wants to launch all service channels at once? (Choose 2)","o":["Agents may not be trained on the new channels","Integration and routing problems could affect customers at scale","Reports will become unavailable","The Salesforce licence will be cancelled","Cases cannot be created"],"a":[0,1],"e":"Big launches increase the chance of unprepared agents and untested routing or integrations. A phased approach reduces risk."},{"id":"ser-1ehmaug","d":"industry","m":false,"q":"A company has a contact centre where customers have different service levels based on the contract they bought. Which business need does this describe?","o":["Differentiated support commitments, such as entitlements and service level agreements","Lead scoring","Campaign tracking","Territory planning"],"a":[0],"e":"Different support levels are a typical reason for entitlement management and SLAs so that agents know what each customer is owed."},{"id":"ser-18ayp8p","d":"implementation","m":false,"q":"At the start of a service project the consultant wants all stakeholders to share expectations for scope, roles and timeline. What should they create?","o":["A project charter or statement of work agreed with the sponsor","A data load file","A page layout","A list of Apex classes"],"a":[0],"e":"A shared scope document sets expectations, responsibilities and boundaries, which helps manage changes later."},{"id":"ser-121bgcy","d":"implementation","m":false,"q":"A client plans to bring in ten years of case history from a legacy system. Which risk related to data should the consultant raise?","o":["Large data volumes may affect performance and storage, so decide what to migrate and what to archive","The records will lose all their relationships","The cases will not be reportable","Salesforce does not accept historical cases"],"a":[0],"e":"Moving all historic data can drive up storage, slow list views and reports, and increase load time. A selective migration and archiving plan keeps the org responsive."},{"id":"ser-eu46mk","d":"implementation","m":false,"q":"Which approach to training best prepares service agents for a new console?","o":["Role-based training with hands-on scenarios in a sandbox and quick reference guides","A single email with a link to documentation","Training only for managers","No training and rely on peers"],"a":[0],"e":"Agents learn best with practice in realistic scenarios that match their daily work, supported by short guides to use afterwards."},{"id":"ser-k5nj0m","d":"implementation","m":false,"q":"A global company wants consistent data quality across regions. Which activity belongs to data governance?","o":["Defining data owners, standards and rules for how case and contact data is created and maintained","Choosing the colour of the console","Adding more page layouts","Removing validation rules"],"a":[0],"e":"Governance sets ownership and standards so that data stays reliable as the organisation grows."},{"id":"ser-r6bisj","d":"implementation","m":false,"q":"During go-live planning, which activity helps reduce the impact if a problem appears?","o":["A rollback or contingency plan, and hypercare support from the project team","Release without any checks","Turn off all monitoring","Remove the support team"],"a":[0],"e":"A contingency plan and a period of extra support after launch help the team react quickly to issues."},{"id":"ser-slrwlp","d":"implementation","m":false,"q":"A consultant must decide whether to use a phased delivery or a single release for a service transformation. Which factor favours a phased delivery?","o":["High complexity and many teams that need to adopt new processes","A very small team with one simple process","No change to existing processes","Unlimited budget and time"],"a":[0],"e":"Phasing reduces risk where there are many changes and groups. A simple change for a small team can be released at once."},{"id":"ser-em6ro1","d":"design","m":false,"q":"A company wants agents to see the customer's details, open cases, and knowledge articles in one place while on a call. Which design provides this?","o":["A Service Console app with a customised Lightning page for cases","A standard navigation app with a tab for each object","A Visualforce page for each object","A report on the customer"],"a":[0],"e":"The Service Console is designed for agents to work on many records with split view and utilities, and a Lightning page can bring related information together."},{"id":"ser-ghzfzn","d":"design","m":false,"q":"Customers submit sensitive health information through cases, and only the assigned team should see it. What should the design include?","o":["A private sharing model for cases, field-level security and encryption for the sensitive fields","Making all cases public","Adding the information to the case subject","Removing field-level security"],"a":[0],"e":"A restrictive baseline, targeted access and encryption protect sensitive data. Putting it in a subject line would expose it widely."},{"id":"ser-1nutyq3","d":"design","m":false,"q":"A company wants a customer to see the status of their cases and update them through a web portal. Which solution fits?","o":["An Experience Cloud site with case access for customer users","A public Web-to-Lead form","A Slack channel","A list view in the console"],"a":[0],"e":"Experience Cloud lets external users log in and see their own records, with the sharing model controlling what they can access."},{"id":"ser-mmhepy","d":"design","m":false,"q":"A support team has two types of cases that need different fields and processes. What should be used?","o":["Record types, with page layouts and support processes for each","Two separate orgs","Separate objects for each field","One layout for both with all fields visible"],"a":[0],"e":"Record types allow different picklist values, layouts and processes on the same object."},{"id":"ser-o2jn9a","d":"design","m":true,"q":"Which TWO elements should the consultant consider to design the customer experience for a self-service portal? (Choose 2)","o":["How easily customers can find knowledge articles","When the customer needs to escalate to an agent","The number of Apex classes in the org","The licence expiry date for the admin","The version of the API"],"a":[0,1],"e":"Self-service works when answers are easy to find and a clear path to a person exists when the article does not help."},{"id":"ser-1u1eb3s","d":"design","m":false,"q":"A client requires that agents can only see cases from their own region. What is the most suitable approach?","o":["Set the case default access to Private and use roles or sharing rules by region","Use a list view filter only","Ask agents to avoid other regions","Set the default to Public Read/Write"],"a":[0],"e":"List filters do not enforce security. Sharing and roles control which records an agent can access."},{"id":"ser-1mzea1k","d":"design","m":false,"q":"Which design choice helps reduce the time agents spend entering information on a case?","o":["Quick text and macros that insert common replies and actions","Adding more required fields","Removing the console","Disabling email integration"],"a":[0],"e":"Macros and quick text automate repeated steps and phrases, saving time and keeping answers consistent."},{"id":"ser-ua946q","d":"design","m":false,"q":"A consultant must design a solution that meets a company's compliance rules for retaining case history for seven years. What should be considered?","o":["Retention and archival strategy, field history tracking and storage limits","Deleting cases after one month","Public sharing of cases","Disabling case history"],"a":[0],"e":"Retention rules affect storage, performance and reporting, and the design must keep the required history accessible."},{"id":"ser-pbn025","d":"knowledge","m":false,"q":"What is the correct order of the Knowledge article lifecycle?","o":["Draft, in review or published, then archived","Published, draft, deleted","Archived, draft, published","Draft, deleted, published"],"a":[0],"e":"Articles are created as drafts, may go through review, are published for use and are archived when they are no longer valid."},{"id":"ser-17op9d9","d":"knowledge","m":false,"q":"A company wants to use Knowledge-Centered Service. Which behaviour does the method encourage?","o":["Agents capture and improve articles while solving cases","Only managers write articles","Articles are written after the project has finished","Knowledge is kept separate from case work"],"a":[0],"e":"KCS makes knowledge creation part of the case workflow, so articles are created, reused and improved as problems are solved."},{"id":"ser-11g3b8k","d":"knowledge","m":false,"q":"A company wants customers in different countries to see articles in their language. What should be configured?","o":["Multiple languages for Knowledge, with translations of articles","A different Salesforce org for each country","Separate record types for each language","A custom object for each article"],"a":[0],"e":"Knowledge supports multiple languages, and translated versions are linked to the master article."},{"id":"ser-q0a5r","d":"knowledge","m":true,"q":"Which TWO configurations let agents attach an article to a case? (Choose 2)","o":["Add the Knowledge component to the case page in the console","Enable the Knowledge user permission for the agents","Create a validation rule on Case","Turn on Web-to-Case","Add a report to the page"],"a":[0,1],"e":"Agents need the Knowledge user setting and a Knowledge component on the page to search and attach articles."},{"id":"ser-11ndabf","d":"knowledge","m":false,"q":"A company wants some articles visible only to partners and not to customers. Which feature controls this?","o":["Data categories and channel visibility settings","Page layouts","Lead assignment rules","Case queues"],"a":[0],"e":"Data categories and channels determine which users and audiences see each article."},{"id":"ser-seoqn4","d":"knowledge","m":false,"q":"How can a company measure whether articles are helping customers?","o":["Use article ratings, views and the cases attached to articles in reports","Count the number of articles written","Ask agents to guess","Delete low-use articles"],"a":[0],"e":"Reports on views, ratings and attached cases show the usefulness of knowledge content and where to improve it."},{"id":"ser-12h98yb","d":"channels","m":false,"q":"A company wants customers to be able to email support and have a case created automatically. Which feature is used?","o":["Email-to-Case","Web-to-Lead","Campaigns","Assignment rules for leads"],"a":[0],"e":"Email-to-Case turns incoming emails into cases and keeps the conversation on the case record."},{"id":"ser-1n5on9h","d":"channels","m":false,"q":"A company wants to offer live text chat with agents on its website. Which feature should be used?","o":["Messaging for In-App and Web, routed with Omni-Channel","Chatter groups","Email templates","A custom Visualforce page"],"a":[0],"e":"Messaging channels allow real-time conversation with customers, and Omni-Channel routes the sessions to available agents."},{"id":"ser-1xvb09v","d":"channels","m":false,"q":"Agents are overloaded with some channels while others are idle. Which feature routes work based on agent capacity and priority?","o":["Omni-Channel routing with capacity settings and presence statuses","A public group","A manual assignment by managers","A scheduled report"],"a":[0],"e":"Omni-Channel pushes work items to agents according to their availability and capacity, balancing load across the team."},{"id":"ser-97cvqq","d":"channels","m":false,"q":"A company wants an AI agent to answer common questions on the website and hand off to a person when needed. What should the consultant explain?","o":["An Agentforce service agent can handle routine requests and escalate to a human through Omni-Channel","AI agents cannot connect to knowledge","Escalation is impossible","The agent must be a Visualforce page"],"a":[0],"e":"A service agent can resolve common questions using knowledge and actions, and a handoff passes the conversation and context to a human when the agent cannot help."},{"id":"ser-1elqqi1","d":"channels","m":true,"q":"Which TWO considerations are important when planning a voice channel? (Choose 2)","o":["Telephony integration and call routing rules","Agent training on handling calls within the console","Page layout colours","The number of Apex triggers","The number of dashboards"],"a":[0,1],"e":"Voice depends on telephony and routing, and agents need to be comfortable handling calls alongside cases."},{"id":"ser-rmhzjk","d":"channels","m":false,"q":"A company wants to capture web inquiries as cases with a form on its site. Which solution does this with little configuration?","o":["Web-to-Case","Email-to-Lead","Chatter Answers","A report"],"a":[0],"e":"Web-to-Case generates an HTML form that creates cases from submissions, with a limit on the number of cases per day."},{"id":"ser-13y47oj","d":"channels","m":false,"q":"What is a key design consideration when using many channels for the same customer?","o":["Keeping a single view of the customer and conversation history across channels","Using a different contact record for each channel","Making agents search separate systems","Deleting messages after each session"],"a":[0],"e":"A unified history lets agents see previous contacts so the customer does not have to repeat information."},{"id":"ser-1afr2h3","d":"cases","m":false,"q":"A company wants new cases to go to the right team based on case type and priority. Which feature should be used?","o":["Case assignment rules, or Omni-Channel flows, with queues","A validation rule","A lookup filter","A report subscription"],"a":[0],"e":"Rules and flows evaluate case data and place the case in a queue or assign it to an owner."},{"id":"ser-1yosw9z","d":"cases","m":false,"q":"A client needs to guarantee a response within two hours for premium customers. Which Salesforce features are used to set this up?","o":["Entitlements, entitlement processes and milestones with business hours","Lead conversion","Campaign hierarchies","Quote templates"],"a":[0],"e":"Entitlements define what support a customer is owed, and milestones in an entitlement process track the response times against business hours."},{"id":"ser-acpdrd","d":"cases","m":false,"q":"What happens when a case milestone is not completed before its target time?","o":["A violation action can run, for example notifying a manager or escalating the case","The case is deleted","Nothing is ever recorded","The customer is blocked"],"a":[0],"e":"Milestones can have actions on warning and violation, such as sending email or updating a field, so the team can react to missed targets."},{"id":"ser-1ps9374","d":"cases","m":true,"q":"Which TWO items can be tied to an entitlement to describe the service a customer receives? (Choose 2)","o":["A service contract","An asset or product covered by support","A lead source","A campaign","A report folder"],"a":[0,1],"e":"Entitlements connect to accounts, contacts, assets and service contracts to define coverage."},{"id":"ser-18yi62t","d":"cases","m":false,"q":"A support manager wants to move aged cases to a manager automatically when they stay unresolved. Which feature supports this?","o":["Case escalation rules","Page layouts","Lookup relationships","A validation rule"],"a":[0],"e":"Escalation rules reassign and notify when cases meet age criteria without action, using business hours."},{"id":"ser-yf6qdq","d":"cases","m":false,"q":"How can a company encourage customers to find solutions before opening a case?","o":["Show suggested articles while the customer enters the case subject on the site","Remove the contact form","Force customers to call","Hide the knowledge base"],"a":[0],"e":"Suggesting relevant articles while the customer types can resolve the issue and avoid a case, which is the idea behind deflection."},{"id":"ser-18v496w","d":"cases","m":false,"q":"A company wants to automate the creation of a follow-up task when a case is closed with a specific reason. What should the admin use?","o":["A record-triggered flow on the Case object","A workflow on the Lead object","A Chatter post","A page layout"],"a":[0],"e":"Record-triggered flows can create tasks or records when case field values meet criteria, and they are the recommended automation tool."},{"id":"ser-1cmcccc","d":"analytics","m":false,"q":"A service manager wants to see open cases by priority and age in a visual format that updates automatically. What should the admin build?","o":["A dashboard with components based on case reports","A static spreadsheet","A Chatter feed","A custom object"],"a":[0],"e":"Dashboards visualise report data, and they can be refreshed on a schedule."},{"id":"ser-1601mh5","d":"analytics","m":false,"q":"A report is needed that lists cases with their related Knowledge articles. What should the admin use?","o":["A custom report type that links Cases with Case Articles","A formula field","A list view","A dashboard filter"],"a":[0],"e":"Standard report types may not combine objects the way a request requires, so a custom report type defines the relationships."},{"id":"ser-1gz45vq","d":"analytics","m":false,"q":"A manager wants each regional lead to see the same dashboard but with only their region's data. Which feature supports this?","o":["A dynamic dashboard that runs as the viewing user","A dashboard that runs as the manager for everyone","A copy of the dashboard for each region","A public report folder"],"a":[0],"e":"Dynamic dashboards show data according to the viewing user's access, so each person sees the records they are allowed to see."},{"id":"ser-2wzwly","d":"analytics","m":true,"q":"Which TWO metrics help evaluate agent productivity in a contact centre? (Choose 2)","o":["Average handle time","Cases closed per agent","Opportunity amount","Campaign cost","Lead source"],"a":[0,1],"e":"Handle time and the number of cases closed by each agent show workload and efficiency. Sales and marketing measures do not apply."},{"id":"ser-1h83g9h","d":"analytics","m":false,"q":"A supervisor wants a real-time view of which agents are available and which queues are busy. What should be used?","o":["Omni Supervisor","A weekly report","The setup audit trail","A Chatter group"],"a":[0],"e":"Omni Supervisor shows the live status of agents and work in queues so that supervisors can monitor and respond."},{"id":"ser-1ribrv","d":"analytics","m":false,"q":"A client wants to share a snapshot of a dashboard with executives every Monday. What can the admin do?","o":["Schedule the dashboard refresh and email it to the recipients","Ask someone to take a screenshot","Export all cases to a file","Create a new dashboard every week"],"a":[0],"e":"Dashboards can be scheduled to refresh and email on a recurring basis, which saves manual work."},{"id":"ser-1www538","d":"integrations","m":false,"q":"A company wants agents to see order data from an external system on the case page without storing it in Salesforce. Which approach should the consultant suggest?","o":["External objects with Salesforce Connect, or an embedded component that queries the system","Import all orders into Salesforce nightly","Ask agents to switch to another browser tab","Export orders to a spreadsheet"],"a":[0],"e":"Salesforce Connect shows external data in real time as external objects without copying it, which avoids duplicate storage and stale information."},{"id":"ser-1v7adr1","d":"integrations","m":false,"q":"A company wants its telephone system to open the customer record when a call arrives. What should be used?","o":["A computer-telephony integration through Open CTI or a certified partner adapter","A Web-to-Case form","A scheduled flow","An email template"],"a":[0],"e":"CTI integrations connect telephony to the console so that incoming calls can screen-pop the matching customer record."},{"id":"ser-aaf2x1","d":"integrations","m":false,"q":"Which factor is important when choosing between a real-time integration and a batch integration?","o":["How current the data must be, and the volume and limits of the systems","The colour theme of the console","The number of dashboards","The name of the org"],"a":[0],"e":"Real-time integration is suited to data that agents need immediately, while batch integration suits large volumes where a delay is acceptable."},{"id":"ser-xp3wvh","d":"integrations","m":false,"q":"A customer wants to share a case with an external partner in another Salesforce org. Which feature supports this?","o":["Salesforce to Salesforce or a connected sharing approach for cross-org records","Chatter free users","A public report","An email attachment only"],"a":[0],"e":"Cross-org record sharing is supported through designed features, so the partner sees the shared case in its own org."}]}};
